he boundary's durable write is a checkpoint capture, a journal transition, a receipt or a marker (rows whose durable facts belong to unlanded owners — lease persistence beyond sessrepo, terminal creation, provider process start, bridge launch — are recorded as NOT APPLICABLE with the exact owner named, never silently skipped) — inject (a) a crash after the boundary's durable write and before the next phase and (b) where an external effect exists, a crash after the effect may have happened and before its result is durable, using real child-process termination (SIGKILL at the seam, the sessckpt crash_unix pattern) and the landed hooks, then perform a clean restart and run the recovery evaluator, asserting exactly one outcome with the full conformance record the gate requires (boundary ID, path, operation IDs, pre/post durable facts, external effect and status probe, winning lease before/after, native identity/binding before/after, selected outcome, evidence satisfying it) and the mutual-exclusion/exhaustiveness rules (contradictory or missing evidence must select recoverable_parked_state; no fourth outcome; no unclassified successful restart); include the rejection cases (two live authorities for one logical session, unfenced external continuation, recovery invoking a new-session launch / fresh native handle / relabelled blank state / different realm — each must be refused as any outcome); cover both direct and task-board paths per boundary where the plan phase applies; prove the Section 13.12 rows the harness can reach (operator interrupt preserving the journal, owner-resume response lost preserving the prepared journal with no second process, atomic rename blocked, disk full via a fault-injecting filesystem, task-board import/open/adopt failure before/after the new lease). Ship the harness as Go tests plus a table-driven boundary registry derived from the pinned Section 13.13 table by a derivation test (not a hand-typed list), a machine-readable conformance record per boundary written under .temp during the run and attached in the evidence tarball, narrowing mutants for the evaluator's classification predicates and every rejection rule with an applied harmless SURVIVED control, and a conformance matrix mapping each 13.12/13.13 clause and each boundary ID to a test row, a NOT APPLICABLE row with owner, or a stated bound. No product behavior change is expected; if a boundary exposes a defect in sessckpt/matjournal, fix it minimally in this leaf with a RED-first regression and say so. This is the FINAL leaf (story_final CR): carry the Story-close items — the traceability registry bindings for 13.12/13.13 (currently 13.12 unmeasured) updated to the real conformance harness with honest coverage text and acceptance cases, reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256 re-pinned; README package sections (sessckpt and matjournal exist; add yours) with test commands and no capability claim; LOGBOOK entry. Managed Story worktree contract: .temp/STORY-260830-2rqigd/worktree on branch task-board/story/STORY-260830-2rqigd whose tip is the 3k3e6m checkpoint; leave the candidate UNCOMMITTED, never commit on the Story branch, never edit .task-board directly, never self-accept; if origin/main moves before your handoff (it will: a release-agnostic validation command is landing on trunk), run task-board worktree refresh-candidate TASK-260830-17ootk and restore any trunk-changed path the refresh left stale with a single-path git checkout HEAD -- <path> (task-board.config.json in particular must equal HEAD); before handoff verify git status shows only candidate paths (no __pycache__, no .pyc). Evidence contract as in the repository DoD. Read the Curator-managed go-testing-tools skill first; all CI local; run the full configured validation suite once before the handoff; hand off no later than 3.5 hours in (a 13-point leaf: if the full registry cannot be finished, hand off a reviewable slice with the remaining boundaries enumerated precisely — but the Story-close items are mandatory). Attach TASK-260830-17ootk_results.md, TASK-260830-17ootk_conformance-matrix.md and TASK-260830-17ootk_producer-evidence.tar.gz (a real gzip archive), keep the checklist current, then task-board handoff TASK-260830-17ootk --role developer and exit promptly. Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board. Model: muse-spark max. The independent reviewer will be muse-spark xhigh while codex is out of quota.","final_result":true}}}
