{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4bb","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae2b-f4bb-7310-a5c5-e45123d43dca"},"sequence":184,"recorded_at":1780531400000363,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"f3ccc2af-522d-4b28-99ba-3a506c9bdcb3","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"f3ccc2af-522d-4b28-99ba-3a506c9bdcb3","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"f3ccc2af-522d-4b28-99ba-3a506c9bdcb3"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ae2c-a334-7520-8bc2-053c56ec62c9"},"task_id":"01a0ae2c-a334-7520-8bc2-053c56ec62c9","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0ae2c-a334-7520-8bc2-053c56ec62c9","chunk":"Read text file `internal/matjournal/doc.go`.\n1|// Package matjournal persists the Materialization Journal 2.0.0 recovery\n2|// contract over prepare, staging, validation, commit, and rollback\n3|// (STORY-260830-2rqigd, TASK-260830-3k3e6m).\n4|//\n5|// Authority: relux-works/agent-session-manager-spec@v0.6.0, Section 10.6\n6|// (Materialization Journal), Section 10.5 (Materialization Plan, referenced\n7|// immutable input), Section 13.12 (failure matrix), and Section 13.13\n8|// (crash/restart outcome gate). The task scope cites the same section\n9|// numbers of v0.5.0; the headings are retained in v0.6.0.\n10|//\n11|// The package owns the mutable journal document, its phase machine, the\n12|// prepare receipt, and the status-first recovery evaluator. It reuses the\n13|// landed shared owners and never duplicates them:\n14|//\n15|//   - internal/canonicaljson owns canonical JSON (Canonicalize) for the\n16|//     prepare-request digest and the marker omit-self digest. The closed\n17|//     journal/marker shapes are validated in this package: the shape owner\n18|//     still registers materialization-journal 2.0.0 (and\n19|//     materialization-plan 1.0.0) with rejectUnsupportedImmutableObjectShape,\n20|//     and its census and inventory suites pin that registration, so replacing\n21|//     it is outside this leaf's scope. The plan itself stays an opaque\n22|//     digest input; only its authority routing view is cross-checked.\n23|//   - internal/scalar owns digest, UUID, timestamp, path, and provider-id\n24|//     grammar.\n25|//   - internal/environ owns strict object decode and extension keys.\n26|//   - internal/axerror owns the Structured Error recorded as last_error\n27|//     (cause kept off the wire by construction) and the stable codes that\n28|//     classify recovery outcomes.\n29|//   - internal/sessckpt owns the operation-receipt discipline this journal\n30|//     adopts: an operation-keyed, input-digest-compared, no-replace receipt\n31|//     installed after the bytes it names. The prepare receipt is a distinct\n32|//     record from a checkpoint-capture receipt (different operation\n33|//     namespace, different idempotency key and digest), documented in\n34|//     TRACEABILITY.md; the install order and replay rules are shared.\n35|//   - internal/secconftest owns the crash-injection vocabulary the tests\n36|//     wire to the store hooks. Product code never imports it.\n37|//\n38|// Refusal taxonomy:\n39|//\n40|//   - ErrInvalidJournal reports a journal shape or transition the contract\n41|//     refuses: malformed grammar, closed-shape violations, token-state\n42|//     violations, ID drift, illegal phase or sub-state transitions, and\n43|//     torn durable bytes.\n44|//   - ErrJournalConflict reports the idempotency boundary: the same\n45|//     operation retried with a byte-unequal body (idempotency_mismatch),\n46|//     or a digest path holding disagreeing bytes (a torn store).\n47|//   - ErrUnknownJournal reports a materialization with no journal.\n48|//     Callers distinguish absence (this error) from torn state (the\n49|//     invalid class) and from a store failure (the wrapped operational\n50|//     error).\n51|//\n52|// Durable-write model (TASK-260830-3qrfjp, as in sessckpt/sessrepo):\n53|// immutable sidecars (plan view, prepare receipt) install no-replace\n54|// (O_EXCL) with fsync before close; the mutable journal installs O_EXCL\n55|// at creation and moves through atomic replace (same-directory temp\n56|// file, fsync, rename, directory sync) afterwards, following the Section\n57|// 10.6 current-marker discipline. Directory fsync follows every install.\n58|// A crash leaves either nothing, or complete bytes that re-validate;\n59|// an interrupted operation resumes by retrying the same IDs with a\n60|// byte-identical body (safe_retry), never by inventing state.\n61|//\n62|// Stated bounds: no CLI, no Mesh RPC, no provider plugin or bridge\n63|// process — provider/bridge/marker/lease/native states arrive as modeled\n64|// status inputs to Recover. Filesystem staging removal and predecessor\n65|// restoration are coordinator work; the journal records the converged\n66|// states. Marker history/current files belong to the replica owner;\n67|// this package validates marker bytes and classifies destinations.\n68|package matjournal","final_result":true}}}
