{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4bf","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae2b-f4bb-7310-a5c5-e45123d43dca"},"sequence":186,"recorded_at":1780531400000367,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"f3ccc2af-522d-4b28-99ba-3a506c9bdcb3","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"f3ccc2af-522d-4b28-99ba-3a506c9bdcb3","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"f3ccc2af-522d-4b28-99ba-3a506c9bdcb3"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ae2c-a2dc-7270-a7bd-0d8e4229c774"},"task_id":"01a0ae2c-a2dc-7270-a7bd-0d8e4229c774","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0ae2c-a2dc-7270-a7bd-0d8e4229c774","chunk":"Read text file `internal/sessckpt/doc.go`.\n1|// Package sessckpt captures typed Checkpoint Record 1.0.0 closures over\n2|// provider identity, workspace manifests, the task-board bundle, terminal\n3|// evidence, and the source head (STORY-260830-2rqigd, TASK-260830-14yo67).\n4|//\n5|// Authority: relux-works/agent-session-manager-spec@v0.6.0, Sections 5.4\n6|// (Checkpoint Record), 10.5-10.6 (Materialization Plan/Journal closure\n7|// inputs), and 13.12-13.13 (failure matrix and crash/restart outcome\n8|// gate). The task scope cites the same section numbers of v0.5.0; the\n9|// headings are retained in v0.6.0.\n10|//\n11|// The package owns capture and durable install only. It reuses the\n12|// landed shared owners and never duplicates them:\n13|//\n14|//   - internal/canonicaljson owns the closed Checkpoint Record shape\n15|//     and the canonical omit-self digest (checkpoint_id).\n16|//   - internal/sessrepo owns record attestation\n17|//     (AttestCheckpointRecord) and the event chain the source head\n18|//     binds against (ListEvents).\n19|//   - internal/sessquery owns semantic admission (admitCheckpoint:\n20|//     owning lease tuple, creator-holder, persistence variant, event\n21|//     heads at or before the owning lease). Capture pre-checks the\n22|//     variant and head binding it can decide from its inputs so an\n23|//     unpublishable closure is refused before publication, but the\n24|//     admission verdict stays with the consumer; tests drive the\n25|//     consumer on captured records instead of re-implementing it.\n26|//   - internal/scalar owns digest, UUID, and timestamp grammar.\n27|//   - internal/secconftest owns the crash-injection vocabulary the\n28|//     tests wire to the store hooks.\n29|//\n30|// Refusal taxonomy (SPEC Section 5.4: CP-N1..CP-N4 MUST be rejected\n31|// with incompatible_schema before publication):\n32|//\n33|//   - ErrInvalidCheckpoint wraps canonicaljson.ErrInvalidIdentity, so\n34|//     errors.Is proves the incompatible_schema class for every\n35|//     unpublishable closure: malformed grammar, closed-shape\n36|//     violations, non-quiescent terminal evidence, missing or\n37|//     doubled persistence members, the wrong persistence variant\n38|//     for the declared session kind, and heads that postdate the\n39|//     owning lease.\n40|//   - Unknown sessions and unknown heads propagate the sessrepo\n41|//     chain-read errors (ErrUnknownSession, ErrUnknownEvent), so\n42|//     errors.Is preserves the owner's vocabulary.\n43|//   - ErrCheckpointConflict reports the idempotency boundary: the\n44|//     same operation retried with moved inputs, and a digest path\n45|//     holding disagreeing bytes.\n46|//\n47|// Durable-write model (TASK-260830-3qrfjp): content-addressed blobs\n48|// installed no-replace (O_EXCL) with fsync before close, operation\n49|// receipts installed no-replace after the blob they name, directory\n50|// fsync after install. A crash leaves either nothing, or complete\n51|// bytes that verify through the canonical owner; an interrupted\n52|// capture is resumed by retrying the same operation with\n53|// byte-identical inputs (safe_retry), never by inventing state.\n54|//\n55|// Stated bounds: the raw AdmitRecord path attests shape and the\n56|// variant/head gates it can decide, but chain binding needs the\n57|// caller's repository handle; a nil chain refuses closed rather\n58|// than skipping the gate. Capture does not consult lease records:\n59|// creator-holder binding is decided by the consumer at admission\n60|// (pinned by tests here). Capture performs no provider or\n61|// task-board I/O and offers no CLI surface.\n62|package sessckpt","final_result":true}}}
