{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4cb","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae2b-f4bb-7310-a5c5-e45123d43dca"},"sequence":192,"recorded_at":1780531400000379,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"f3ccc2af-522d-4b28-99ba-3a506c9bdcb3","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"f3ccc2af-522d-4b28-99ba-3a506c9bdcb3","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"f3ccc2af-522d-4b28-99ba-3a506c9bdcb3"},"call_id":"call_01a0ae2c9a1a76b8a0856dbea1735f69","text":"Read text file `internal/sessckpt/doc.go`.\n1|// Package sessckpt captures typed Checkpoint Record 1.0.0 closures over\n2|// provider identity, workspace manifests, the task-board bundle, terminal\n3|// evidence, and the source head (STORY-260830-2rqigd, TASK-260830-14yo67).\n4|//\n5|// Authority: relux-works/agent-session-manager-spec@v0.6.0, Sections 5.4\n6|// (Checkpoint Record), 10.5-10.6 (Materialization Plan/Journal closure\n7|// inputs), and 13.12-13.13 (failure matrix and crash/restart outcome\n8|// gate). The task scope cites the same section numbers of v0.5.0; the\n9|// headings are retained in v0.6.0.\n10|//\n11|// The package owns capture and durable install only. It reuses the\n12|// landed shared owners and never duplicates them:\n13|//\n14|//   - internal/canonicaljson owns the closed Checkpoint Record shape\n15|//     and the canonical omit-self digest (checkpoint_id).\n16|//   - internal/sessrepo owns record attestation\n17|//     (AttestCheckpointRecord) and the event chain the source head\n18|//     binds against (ListEvents).\n19|//   - internal/sessquery owns semantic admission (admitCheckpoint:\n20|//     owning lease tuple, creator-holder, persistence variant, event\n21|//     heads at or before the owning lease). Capture pre-checks the\n22|//     variant and head binding it can decide from its inputs so an\n23|//     unpublishable closure is refused before publication, but the\n24|//     admission verdict stays with the consumer; tests drive the\n25|//     consumer on captured records instead of re-implementing it.\n26|//   - internal/scalar owns digest, UUID, and timestamp grammar.\n27|//   - internal/secconftest owns the crash-injection vocabulary the\n28|//     tests wire to the store hooks.\n29|//\n30|// Refusal taxonomy (SPEC Section 5.4: CP-N1..CP-N4 MUST be rejected\n31|// with incompatible_schema before publication):\n32|//\n33|//   - ErrInvalidCheckpoint wraps canonicaljson.ErrInvalidIdentity, so\n34|//     errors.Is proves the incompatible_schema class for every\n35|//     unpublishable closure: malformed grammar, closed-shape\n36|//     violations, non-quiescent terminal evidence, missing or\n37|//     doubled persistence members, the wrong persistence variant\n38|//     for the declared session kind, and heads that postdate the\n39|//     owning lease.\n40|//   - Unknown sessions and unknown heads propagate the sessrepo\n41|//     chain-read errors (ErrUnknownSession, ErrUnknownEvent), so\n42|//     errors.Is preserves the owner's vocabulary.\n43|//   - ErrCheckpointConflict reports the idempotency boundary: the\n44|//     same operation retried with moved inputs, and a digest path\n45|//     holding disagreeing bytes.\n46|//\n47|// Durable-write model (TASK-260830-3qrfjp): content-addressed blobs\n48|// installed no-replace (O_EXCL) with fsync before close, operation\n49|// receipts installed no-replace after the blob they name, directory\n50|// fsync after install. A crash leaves either nothing, or complete\n51|// bytes that verify through the canonical owner; an interrupted\n52|// capture is resumed by retrying the same operation with\n53|// byte-identical inputs (safe_retry), never by inventing state.\n54|//\n55|// Stated bounds: the raw AdmitRecord path attests shape and the\n56|// variant/head gates it can decide, but chain binding needs the\n57|// caller's repository handle; a nil chain refuses closed rather\n58|// than skipping the gate. Capture does not consult lease records:\n59|// creator-holder binding is decided by the consumer at admission\n60|// (pinned by tests here). Capture performs no provider or\n61|// task-board I/O and offers no CLI surface.\n62|package sessckpt","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4cd","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae2b-f4bb-7310-a5c5-e45123d43dca"},"sequence":193,"recorded_at":1780531400000381,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"f3ccc2af-522d-4b28-99ba-3a506c9bdcb3","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"f3ccc2af-522d-4b28-99ba-3a506c9bdcb3","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"f3ccc2af-522d-4b28-99ba-3a506c9bdcb3"},"call_id":"call_01a0ae2c9b7f745089a84fc283f752a6","text":"Read text file `internal/matjournal/doc.go`.\n1|// Package matjournal persists the Materialization Journal 2.0.0 recovery\n2|// contract over prepare, staging, validation, commit, and rollback\n3|// (STORY-260830-2rqigd, TASK-260830-3k3e6m).\n4|//\n5|// Authority: relux-works/agent-session-manager-spec@v0.6.0, Section 10.6\n6|// (Materialization Journal), Section 10.5 (Materialization Plan, referenced\n7|// immutable input), Section 13.12 (failure matrix), and Section 13.13\n8|// (crash/restart outcome gate). The task scope cites the same section\n9|// numbers of v0.5.0; the headings are retained in v0.6.0.\n10|//\n11|// The package owns the mutable journal document, its phase machine, the\n12|// prepare receipt, and the status-first recovery evaluator. It reuses the\n13|// landed shared owners and never duplicates them:\n14|//\n15|//   - internal/canonicaljson owns canonical JSON (Canonicalize) for the\n16|//     prepare-request digest and the marker omit-self digest. The closed\n17|//     journal/marker shapes are validated in this package: the shape owner\n18|//     still registers materialization-journal 2.0.0 (and\n19|//     materialization-plan 1.0.0) with rejectUnsupportedImmutableObjectShape,\n20|//     and its census and inventory suites pin that registration, so replacing\n21|//     it is outside this leaf's scope. The plan itself stays an opaque\n22|//     digest input; only its authority routing view is cross-checked.\n23|//   - internal/scalar owns digest, UUID, timestamp, path, and provider-id\n24|//     grammar.\n25|//   - internal/environ owns strict object decode and extension keys.\n26|//   - internal/axerror owns the Structured Error recorded as last_error\n27|//     (cause kept off the wire by construction) and the stable codes that\n28|//     classify recovery outcomes.\n29|//   - internal/sessckpt owns the operation-receipt discipline this journal\n30|//     adopts: an operation-keyed, input-digest-compared, no-replace receipt\n31|//     installed after the bytes it names. The prepare receipt is a distinct\n32|//     record from a checkpoint-capture receipt (different operation\n33|//     namespace, different idempotency key and digest), documented in\n34|//     TRACEABILITY.md; the install order and replay rules are shared.\n35|//   - internal/secconftest owns the crash-injection vocabulary the tests\n36|//     wire to the store hooks. Product code never imports it.\n37|//\n38|// Refusal taxonomy:\n39|//\n40|//   - ErrInvalidJournal reports a journal shape or transition the contract\n41|//     refuses: malformed grammar, closed-shape violations, token-state\n42|//     violations, ID drift, illegal phase or sub-state transitions, and\n43|//     torn durable bytes.\n44|//   - ErrJournalConflict reports the idempotency boundary: the same\n45|//     operation retried with a byte-unequal body (idempotency_mismatch),\n46|//     or a digest path holding disagreeing bytes (a torn store).\n47|//   - ErrUnknownJournal reports a materialization with no journal.\n48|//     Callers distinguish absence (this error) from torn state (the\n49|//     invalid class) and from a store failure (the wrapped operational\n50|//     error).\n51|//\n52|// Durable-write model (TASK-260830-3qrfjp, as in sessckpt/sessrepo):\n53|// immutable sidecars (plan view, prepare receipt) install no-replace\n54|// (O_EXCL) with fsync before close; the mutable journal installs O_EXCL\n55|// at creation and moves through atomic replace (same-directory temp\n56|// file, fsync, rename, directory sync) afterwards, following the Section\n57|// 10.6 current-marker discipline. Directory fsync follows every install.\n58|// A crash leaves either nothing, or complete bytes that re-validate;\n59|// an interrupted operation resumes by retrying the same IDs with a\n60|// byte-identical body (safe_retry), never by inventing state.\n61|//\n62|// Stated bounds: no CLI, no Mesh RPC, no provider plugin or bridge\n63|// process — provider/bridge/marker/lease/native states arrive as modeled\n64|// status inputs to Recover. Filesystem staging removal and predecessor\n65|// restoration are coordinator work; the journal records the converged\n66|// states. Marker history/current files belong to the replica owner;\n67|// this package validates marker bytes and classifies destinations.\n68|package matjournal","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4cf","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae2b-f4bb-7310-a5c5-e45123d43dca"},"sequence":194,"recorded_at":1780531400000383,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"f3ccc2af-522d-4b28-99ba-3a506c9bdcb3","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"f3ccc2af-522d-4b28-99ba-3a506c9bdcb3","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"f3ccc2af-522d-4b28-99ba-3a506c9bdcb3"},"call_id":"call_01a0ae2c9ce57639866c0d7261c6af34","text":"Read text file `internal/sessckpt/TRACEABILITY.md`.\n1|# `internal/sessckpt` traceability (TASK-260830-14yo67)\n2|\n3|Authority: `relux-works/agent-session-manager-spec@v0.6.0`\n4|(`internal/specpin/v0.6.0.lock.json`, embedded\n5|`internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`). The task scope cites the same\n6|section numbers of v0.5.0; the headings are retained in v0.6.0, so\n7|every row below names the pinned v0.6.0 heading. Historical v0.5.0\n8|behavior is preserved: the closed Checkpoint Record 1.0.0 member\n9|set is unchanged between the two revisions.\n10|\n11|Production entry points: `Store.Capture`, `Store.Admit`,\n12|`Store.Get` (`internal/sessckpt/capture.go`); durable install\n13|(`internal/sessckpt/store.go`). No CLI surface is offered; the\n14|`sessckpt` package is a library only.\n15|\n16|## AC coverage (8 of 8 rows driven through the production entries)\n17|\n18|| # | AC row | Production call site | Named tests |\n19|| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n20|| 1 | Closure over provider identity | `Capture` → `checkBoundary` (provider_id/version) + `provider_manifest_id` leg | `TestCaptureDirectInstallsAttestedRecord`, `TestCaptureTaskBoardVariantInstalls`, `TestCaptureRefusesMalformedClosureMembers/bad_provider_id`, `/empty_provider_version` |\n21|| 2 | Closure over workspace manifests | `Capture` → `checkDigestMember(workspace_manifest_id)` | positives above, `TestCaptureRefusesMalformedClosureMembers/bad_workspace_manifest`, `TestCaptureMovedInputsChangeIdentity` |\n22|| 3 | Closure over task-board bundle | `Capture`/`Admit` → `checkPersistenceVariant` | `TestCaptureTaskBoardVariantInstalls`, `TestCaptureRefusesBadPersistenceVariant` (all five arms), `TestAdmitRefusesMalformedFrames/Admit(bad kind)` |\n23|| 4 | Closure over terminal evidence | `Capture` → `checkBoundary` (evidence enum + quiescence publication rule) | `TestCaptureRefusesNonQuiescentBoundary` (all five arms incl. CP-N1), `TestCaptureRefusesMalformedClosureMembers/bad_evidence` |\n24|| 5 | Closure over source head | `Capture`/`Admit` → `checkHeadBinding`/`checkRawHeadBinding` against `sessrepo.Repository.ListEvents` | `TestCaptureAdmitsThroughWinningLeaseConsumer`, `TestCaptureSuccessorAdmitsThroughConsumer`, `TestCaptureRefusesUnknownSessionAndHead`, `TestCaptureRefusesLaterLeaseHead`, `TestCaptureRefusesMalformedHeads` |\n25|| 6 | Exact contract fixtures and negative/refusal cases | `Capture`, `Admit`, `Get` + `sessrepo.AttestCheckpointRecord` | `TestSpecExampleAttestsThroughConsumerOwner`, `TestCaptureDirectInstallsAttestedRecord` (closed member set equals the normative example), CP-N1 (`cp_n1_background_idle_false`), CP-N2 (`cp_n2_direct_null_provider`), CP-N3 (`cp_n3_both_present`), CP-N4 (`TestAdmitRefusesUnknownSafeBoundaryMember` with benign re-identified control), `TestAdmitRefusesMalformedFrames`, `TestGetRefusesUnknownAndTorn` |\n26|| 7 | Crash/idempotency evidence for durable capture | `Store.install` (blob-first, receipt-second, no-replace) + `BeforeWrite`/`AfterBlob`/`AfterCommit` hooks | `TestCrashBeforeDurableWriteIsSafeRetry`, `TestCrashBetweenBlobAndReceiptResumes`, `TestCrashAfterReceiptReplaysRecordedResult`, `TestCaptureCrashChildSelfTerminates` (real SIGKILL), `TestCaptureWithMovedInputsRefuses`, `TestCaptureRefusesDisagreeingDigestPath`, `TestCaptureReplayIsIdempotent`, `TestCaptureIdenticalClosuresShareIdentity` |\n27|| 8 | No unsupported capability advertised | no `cmd/` surface, no provider/task-board I/O in the package | Stated bound (see below); `gofmt`/`go vet`/`go build` clean, README/doctor untouched by this change |\n28|\n29|## Pinned-clause map\n30|\n31|### Section 5.4 Checkpoint Record\n32|\n33|| Clause | Owner / call site | Evidence |\n34|| --- | --- | --- |\n35|| Closed 16-member shape, `schema`/`schema_version` exact, `status` = `validated`, `subject_id` = `session_id` | `canonicaljson.validateCheckpointRecord` via `sessrepo.AttestCheckpointRecord`; `buildCandidate` assembles exactly the closed set | member-set equality vs the normative example in `TestCaptureDirectInstallsAttestedRecord`; `TestSpecExampleAttestsThroughConsumerOwner` |\n36|| `checkpoint_id` canonical omit-self digest | `canonicaljson.CalculateObjectIdentity` + `AttestCheckpointRecord`, drift-checked in `identifyCandidate` | every positive test attests; `TestAdmitRefusesMalformedFrames/Admit(tampered)` |\n37|| Safe Boundary Evidence closed shape + publication rule (all idle true, counters zero) | `checkBoundary` first, owner backstop second | quiescence table; narrowing mutant `N-bg-idle` killed by `cp_n1_background_idle_false` |\n38|| Persistence variant: exactly one leg; direct↔provider, task_board↔bundle | `checkPersistenceVariant` (+ `checkSessionKind`) first, owner presence backstop second | variant table; mutants `N-both-present`, `N-swapped-direct` killed |\n39|| `event_heads` 1..64 sorted unique, resolving at or before the owning lease | `checkHeads` + `checkHeadBinding`/`checkRawHeadBinding` first, owner shape backstop second | heads table + unknown/later-lease tests; mutant `N-duplicate-heads`, `N-later-epoch-head` killed |\n40|| CP-N1..CP-N4 rejected with `incompatible_schema` before publication | `Capture`/`Admit` refuse `ErrInvalidCheckpoint` wrapping `canonicaljson.ErrInvalidIdentity` (`errors.Is` proves both layers) | rows above; mutant `N-evidence-enum` (token-preserving) killed by `bad_evidence` |\n41|| Normative example | attests through the same owner | `TestSpecExampleAttestsThroughConsumerOwner` (digest pinned) |\n42|| Owning lease tuple, creator-holder, variant, head closure at admission | `sessquery.admitCheckpoint` (landed consumer, not re-implemented) | epoch-1 + successor `BuildPlan`/`Revalidate` positives; wrong-creator refusal (`selector_observation_unavailable`) |\n43|| Force-takeover newest-validated-checkpoint selection | consumer behavior, out of capture scope | Stated bound: capture mints and installs; selection stays with the takeover owner |\n44|\n45|### Sections 10.5-10.6 Materialization Plan / Journal\n46|\n47|The checkpoint contributes its closure digests (`workspace_manifest_id`,\n48|`provider_manifest_id`/`task_board_bundle_id`, checkpoint digest,\n49|lease tuple) as plan source inputs; the plan/journal state machines\n50|are owned by sibling TASK-260830-3k3e6m. Capture binds the exact\n51|digest strings the plan rows consume and refuses to publish a\n52|closure no plan row could select (variant gate). No plan or journal\n53|bytes are written here: stated bound.\n54|\n55|### Sections 13.12-13.13 Failure matrix / crash-outcome gate\n56|\n57|| Applicable row | Capture behavior | Evidence |\n58|| --- | --- | --- |\n59|| Invalid digest/schema | refused before any durable byte (`ErrInvalidCheckpoint`) | all negative tests assert zero writes only where counted (`TestCrashBeforeDurableWriteIsSafeRetry` counts 0/0) |\n60|| Operator interrupt / crash before first byte | nothing mutated; identical retry safe (`safe_retry`) | injector `PointPrepareEnter` test |\n61|| Crash between blob and receipt | complete verifying blob, no receipt; identical retry completes (`safe_retry`) | hook test + real SIGKILL test (`TestCaptureCrashChildSelfTerminates`) |\n62|| Crash after receipt | recorded result replayed, no second identity (`safe_retry` via receipt) | hook test |\n63|| Retry with moved inputs | refuses `ErrCheckpointConflict` (`idempotency_mismatch`), writes nothing | `TestCaptureWithMovedInputsRefuses` + narrowing mutant `N-idempotency-session` killed |\n64|| Disk-full / rename-blocked / permission faults | install errors propagate; no-replace keeps existing blobs; torn bytes refuse attestation on read | Design property on the TASK-260830-3qrfjp durable-write model; torn-read path driven by `TestGetRefusesUnknownAndTorn` and `TestCaptureRefusesDisagreeingDigestPath`. No dedicated ENOSPC fault test in this package: stated bound (storage faults are owned with their fault model by `internal/localstore` + TASK-260830-3qrfjp) |\n65|| Two live owners for one session | out of capture scope (lease arbitration) | Stated bound |\n66|\n67|## Negative-evidence proofs\n68|\n69|Shipped harness: `internal/sessckpt/mutant_harness.py`. Run:\n70|\n71|    PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/sessckpt/mutant_harness.py --log-dir .temp/TASK-260830-14yo67/mutants\n72|\n73|Result on the delivered source: **7 of 7 narrowing mutants killed**,\n74|**1 of 1 harmless SURVIVED controls applied**, 0 NOT_APPLIED, 0\n75|compile/harness failures. Per-plant raw logs (command, return code,\n76|full output) live under the log dir with `summary.json`; the same\n77|logs ship in `TASK-260830-14yo67_producer-evidence.tar.gz`.\n78|\n79|| Plant | Weakening (admits exactly the named member) | Killer |\n80|| --- | --- | --- |\n81|| `N-bg-idle` | quiescence gate passes `background_idle=false` when no process is open | `TestCaptureRefusesNonQuiescentBoundary/cp_n1_background_idle_false` (own-gate message attribution; the owner backstop still refuses with different text) |\n82|| `N-both-present` | presence gate passes both-legs-present | `TestCaptureRefusesBadPersistenceVariant/cp_n3_both_present` (the kind gate then fires with different attribution) |\n83|| `N-swapped-direct` | direct arm passes bundle-only | `TestCaptureRefusesBadPersistenceVariant/swapped_direct_takes_bundle` (clean admission kill: capture succeeds) |\n84|| `N-duplicate-heads` | order gate passes duplicates (`<=` → `<`) | `TestCaptureRefusesMalformedHeads/duplicated` (own-gate `sorted unique` attribution; owner backstop text differs) |\n85|| `N-later-epoch-head` | epoch arm admits heads one epoch past the owner (`>` → `>+1`) | `TestCaptureRefusesLaterLeaseHead` (clean admission kill) |\n86|| `N-idempotency-session` | conflict gate passes moved inputs under the same session | `TestCaptureWithMovedInputsRefuses` (clean admission kill: retry succeeds) |\n87|| `N-evidence-enum` | closed enum admits exactly `provider_gossip`; every searched-for token preserved | `TestCaptureRefusesMalformedClosureMembers/bad_evidence` (own-gate `safe_boundary` attribution) |\n88|| `C-harmless-comment` | comment-only edit | `TestCaptureDirectInstallsAttestedRecord` still passes (SURVIVED) |\n89|\n90|## Stated bounds (not driven, declared)\n91|\n92|1. Raw `Admit` trusts the supplier for lease-tuple/creator truth the\n93|   way any sync-installed record does; the consumer re-decides\n94|   creator-holder at admission. Chain binding is still enforced\n95|   (nil chain refuses closed).\n96|2. Capture performs no provider, task-board, or terminal I/O: the\n97|   quiescence facts are caller-declared and the publication rule is\n98|   enforced on the declaration. Live observation belongs to the\n99|   provider/terminal owners.\n100|3. Manifest bytes are referenced by digest only; manifest resolution\n101|   and Transfer Manifest validation belong to their owners.\n102|4. No CLI, no RPC, no replication bytes are emitted or advertised.\n103|5. The `section:5.4` registry binding in\n104|   `internal/traceability/ownership.v0.6.0.json` still records\n105|   \"checkpoint creation ... is not implemented\". That sentence is\n106|   stale as of this change, but the registry projection digest is\n107|   review-pinned (`reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256`:\n108|   \"ownership claims cannot be self-minted without an explicit\n109|   review of this binding\"), so the registry text is left\n110|   untouched for the review-gated registry maintenance. This\n111|   matrix is the interim clause record.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4d1","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae2b-f4bb-7310-a5c5-e45123d43dca"},"sequence":195,"recorded_at":1780531400000385,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"f3ccc2af-522d-4b28-99ba-3a506c9bdcb3","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"f3ccc2af-522d-4b28-99ba-3a506c9bdcb3","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"f3ccc2af-522d-4b28-99ba-3a506c9bdcb3"},"call_id":"call_01a0ae2c9e7e70219ed8cfa1f818f15f","text":"Read text file `internal/matjournal/TRACEABILITY.md`.\n1|# Materialization Journal Traceability\n2|\n3|Authority: relux-works/agent-session-manager-spec@v0.6.0, Section 10.6\n4|(Materialization Journal), Section 10.5 (Materialization Plan,\n5|referenced immutable input), Section 13.12 (failure matrix), and\n6|Section 13.13 (crash/restart outcome gate). The task scope cites the\n7|same section numbers of v0.5.0; the headings are retained in v0.6.0.\n8|\n9|## Production entries\n10|\n11|| Entry | File | Behavior |\n12||---|---|---|\n13|| `Open` | `store.go` | Binds the owner-only materializations root; the root must be absolute. |\n14|| `Create` | `store.go` | Binds both caller-stable IDs and the canonical request digest before any staging or bridge mutation; installs plan view, journal, and prepare receipt; byte-identical retries replay, moved bodies conflict. |\n15|| `Get` | `store.go` | Returns byte-identical journal bytes, re-validated through the closed shape on every read. |\n16|| `UpdateProvider` | `store.go` | Records one provider transaction state with the token rule and ID binding. |\n17|| `UpdateTaskBoard` | `store.go` | Records one task-board state along the sub-state table with the nullability rules and bridge-key binding. |\n18|| `UpdateAuthority` | `store.go` | Records one authority state along the sub-state table with the rollback-root rules. |\n19|| `RecordProgress` | `store.go` | Merges per-blob chunk sets and whole-blob verifications in staging or validating. |\n20|| `RecordError` | `store.go` | Records the redacted Structured Error without moving the phase. |\n21|| `Transition` | `store.go` | Moves the phase along the table with the entry guards. |\n22|| `Rollback` | `store.go` | Executes the allowed abort: rolling_back first, then converged rolled_back. |\n23|| `Recover` | `recover.go` | Classifies one crashed materialization into exactly one Section 13.13 outcome, executing rollback or provable completions. |\n24|| `ValidateMarker` | `marker.go` | Validates the closed marker shape and attests the omit-self identity. |\n25|| `ClassifyDestination` | `marker.go` | Classifies one destination from its durable facts. |\n26|\n27|## Conformance matrix\n28|\n29|`n of m AC rows driven`: every row below is driven through the named\n30|production entry by the named committed test.\n31|\n32|### Journal shape and prepare (Section 10.6)\n33|\n34|| Spec row | Production | Test |\n35||---|---|---|\n36|| Journal closed 22-member shape, literals, null legs | `Create`, `Get` (`store.go`, `journal.go`) | `TestCreatePersistsJournalAndReceipt` |\n37|| Normative prepared example members | `UpdateProvider`, `UpdateAuthority`, `UpdateTaskBoard`, `Transition` | `TestSpecExampleShapeDrivesThroughProduction` |\n38|| MJ-TASK-BOARD-OPENED-POS verbatim fixture | `UpdateTaskBoard` | `TestOpenedFixtureMatchesProduction` |\n39|| Import/open/adopt/resume operation-ID allocation with the materialization ID; no second manager | `Create` | `TestCreatePersistsJournalAndReceipt`, `TestCreateReplayAndConflict` |\n40|| Same IDs plus byte-identical body replay; moved body refuses idempotency_mismatch (MJ-RPC-PREPARE-LOST) | `Create` (`replayCreateLocked`) | `TestCreateReplayAndConflict` |\n41|| Second prepare for one materialization refuses | `Create` | `TestCreateReplayAndConflict` |\n42|| Malformed closure members refuse the invalid class | `Create` (`buildCreate`) | `TestCreateRefusesMalformedClosure` |\n43|| Unknown/absent journal and torn bytes | `Get` | `TestGetRefusals` |\n44|\n45|### Phase machine (Section 10.6, derived table)\n46|\n47|The pinned text names the phase enum and the coordinator order but no\n48|explicit edge table; the table in `legalTransitions` derives one edge\n49|per order step (prepare creates staging, transfer stages, validation\n50|validates, commit returns prepared, finalize commits), one abort edge\n51|per non-terminal phase (a valid staging transaction resumes or rolls\n52|back), and one failure edge per non-terminal phase. The\n53|committing-to-rolling_back edge additionally requires pre-activation\n54|(byte rollback is forbidden after adopt). Each edge is proved by the\n55|walk tests and the full illegal-pair battery.\n56|\n57|| Spec row | Production | Test |\n58||---|---|---|\n59|| Every legal edge admits | `Transition` | `TestSpecExampleShapeDrivesThroughProduction`, `TestFullDormantWalkCommits`, `TestRollbackConverges` |\n60|| Every illegal pair refuses with the table message | `Transition` | `TestTransitionRefusesIllegalEdges` |\n61|| Prepared requires provider prepared and opened bridge durable | `Transition` (`checkTransitionGuards`) | `TestTransitionGuards/prepared_requires_opened`, `prepared_requires_provider_prepared` |\n62|| Committed requires converged sub-states, resumed/dormant bridge, authorities committed, exact destination marker for workspace | `Transition` | `TestTransitionGuards/committed_requires_convergence`, `committed_workspace_requires_marker`, `committed_rejects_drifting_marker` |\n63|| Failed requires the explaining last_error | `Transition` | `TestTransitionGuards/failed_requires_error`, `TestLastErrorIsRedactedStructuredError` |\n64|| Terminal phases freeze every entry | `update` | `TestTerminalFreezes`, `TestTransitionRefusesIllegalEdges` |\n65|\n66|### Provider, bridge, authority rules (Sections 10.6, 7.5)\n67|\n68|| Spec row | Production | Test |\n69||---|---|---|\n70|| Prepared requires a token; every other state requires null | `UpdateProvider` | `TestProviderTokenAndIDRules` |\n71|| Token base64url-256+ grammar (fixpoint, 32..512 bytes) | `checkToken` | `TestProviderTokenAndIDRules`, `TestTokenFixturesAreWellFormed` |\n72|| Transaction authority closed shape and mat/tx/plan binding | `UpdateProvider` | `TestProviderTokenAndIDRules/authority_ids_bind` |\n73|| Transaction ID stable; per-call operation ID may advance | `UpdateProvider` | `TestProviderTokenAndIDRules/transaction_drift_refuses`, `operation_id_may_advance` |\n74|| Bridge null/state invariants per state | `UpdateTaskBoard` | `TestBoardNullabilityRefusals` |\n75|| Bridge sub-state table incl. no adopted rollback | `UpdateTaskBoard` | `TestBoardNullabilityRefusals/subtable_*` |\n76|| Dormant cleanup_after equals the consumed open expiry | `UpdateTaskBoard` | `TestBoardNullabilityRefusals/dormant_expiry_binds_consumed`, `TestFullDormantWalkCommits` |\n77|| Failed preserves only one still-valid pair | `UpdateTaskBoard` | `TestBoardNullabilityRefusals/failed_*` |\n78|| Bridge operation-ID drift refuses | `UpdateTaskBoard` (`checkTaskBoardDrift`) | `TestBoardNullabilityRefusals/operation_drift_refuses` |\n79|| Authority sub-table, rollback-root rules, single provider backup | `UpdateAuthority` | `TestAuthorityGuards` |\n80|| Per-blob chunk sets merge by union (MJ-MULTIBLOB-POS) | `RecordProgress` | `TestRecordProgressMergesPerBlob` |\n81|| Progress closes after validation | `RecordProgress` | `TestRecordProgressMergesPerBlob` |\n82|| Rollback converges tokens, states, and the terminal failure; refuses past activation and without a failure | `Rollback` | `TestRollbackConverges`, `TestTransitionGuards/rollback_refused_*` |\n83|\n84|### Marker and destination (Section 10.6)\n85|\n86|| Spec row | Production | Test |\n87||---|---|---|\n88|| Normative marker example validates; marker_id recomputes | `ValidateMarker` | `TestMarkerExampleValidates` |\n89|| Marker binding (replica, plan, checkpoint, materialization, predecessor) | `Transition`, `Recover` (`checkMarkerBinding`) | `TestTransitionGuards/committed_rejects_drifting_marker`, `TestRecoverCompletesCommit` |\n90|| Destination classes incl. MARKER-* rows | `ClassifyDestination` | `TestClassifyDestination` |\n91|\n92|### Recovery (Sections 13.12, 13.13)\n93|\n94|| Spec row | Production | Test |\n95||---|---|---|\n96|| CR-MAT-01..08, each with a real crash injection followed by `Recover` | `Recover` | `TestCrash*` (8 boundaries), `TestCreateCrashChildSelfTerminates` (SIGKILL) |\n97|| MJ-CRASH-STAGE/PREPARE-LOST/COMMIT-LOST/ROLLBACK-LOST/MARKER-MISMATCH | `Recover` | `TestCrashAfterTransferResumes`, `TestCrashAfterProviderPreparePersistsToken`, `TestRecoverResumes/committing_retries_commit`, `TestRecoverCompletesCommit`, `TestRecoverRollbackRequired`, `TestRecoverGatesPark/marker_mismatch` |\n98|| TB-TXN IMPORT/OPEN/ADOPT/RESUME-LOST, BINDING-MISMATCH, TOKEN-EXPIRED, PASSIVE | `Recover` | `TestRecoverResumes/bridge_*`, `TestRecoverGatesPark/binding_mismatch`, `TestRecoverRollbackRequired/token_expired_before_lease`, `TestFullDormantWalkCommits`, `TestRecoverCompletesCommit/dormant_finalize_closes` |\n99|| 13.12 disk full / rename blocked park with remediation | `Recover` | `TestRecoverGatesPark/disk_full`, `rename_blocked` |\n100|| 13.12 owner-resume lost finalizes under the same IDs | `Recover` | `TestRecoverFailureMatrixRows/owner_resume_lost_finalizes` |\n101|| 13.12 operator interrupt retries the same operation | `Recover` | `TestRecoverFailureMatrixRows/operator_interrupt_retries_same_operation` |\n102|| 13.12 import/open/adopt fail before the lease rolls back | `Recover` | `TestRecoverRollbackRequired/bridge_failed_before_lease`, `token_expired_before_lease` |\n103|| 13.12 adopt fails after the lease stays the stopped owner | `Recover` | `TestRecoverFailureMatrixRows/adopt_fails_after_lease_stays_stopped_owner` |\n104|| Rejection gates: moved/unknown lease, substitution, two live authorities, unfenced continuation, marker integrity, unknown decisive status, token/binding contradiction, torn progression | `Recover` | `TestRecoverGatesPark`, `TestRecoverTornJournalParks`, `TestRecoverContradictoryProgressionParks` |\n105|| Terminal journals replay; park leaves them frozen | `Recover` | `TestRecoverTerminalReplays` |\n106|| Parked/rollback evidence durable with lease, IDs, identity, error; never a fourth outcome | `Recover` (`park`, `completeRollback`) | `TestParkedEvidenceIsDurable`, `mustOutcome` (every recovery test) |\n107|\n108|## Mutants\n109|\n110|Run: `python3 internal/matjournal/mutant_harness.py`. All narrowing\n111|mutants are KILLED; the harmless control SURVIVES. No gate inspects\n112|source text: every gate is a value, table, or grammar comparison, so\n113|the token-preserving requirement holds structurally — the table\n114|mutants (N-phase-table, N-board-subtable) preserve every literal and\n115|change only the edge set.\n116|\n117|| Mutant | Weakening | Killer |\n118||---|---|---|\n119|| N-phase-table | Admits staging-to-committed | `TestTransitionRefusesIllegalEdges` |\n120|| N-board-subtable | Admits not_started-to-opened | `TestBoardNullabilityRefusals/subtable_refuses_skip` |\n121|| N-provider-token | Admits prepared-without-token | `TestProviderTokenAndIDRules/prepared_requires_token` |\n122|| N-board-import | Admits expiry-less imports | `TestBoardNullabilityRefusals/imported_triple_incomplete` |\n123|| N-id-drift-adopt | Admits adopt-ID drift | `TestBoardNullabilityRefusals/operation_drift_refuses` |\n124|| N-create-first-prepare | Admits different-operation same-body replay | `TestCreateReplayAndConflict` |\n125|| N-rollback-adopt | Admits adopted rollback | `TestTransitionGuards/rollback_refused_after_adopt` |\n126|| N-failed-null | Admits explicit-null explaining error | `TestTransitionGuards/failed_requires_error` |\n127|| N-commit-marker | Admits marker-less commits on journals with authorities | `TestTransitionGuards/committed_workspace_requires_marker` |\n128|| N-recover-uncertain-floor | Admits unrecorded-prepare unknown probes at CR-MAT-05..07 | `TestParkedEvidenceIsDurable` |\n129|| N-token-length | Admits exactly 3-byte tokens | `TestProviderTokenAndIDRules/short_token_refuses` |\n130|| C-doc-comment | Comment-only control | `TestTokenFixturesAreWellFormed` (SURVIVES) |\n131|\n132|## Receipt reconciliation\n133|\n134|The prepare receipt adopts the sessckpt operation-receipt discipline —\n135|an operation-keyed, input-digest-compared, no-replace receipt installed\n136|after the bytes it names — and is a distinct record because it binds\n137|the materialize.prepare namespace (prepare operation, canonical\n138|request body, journal) rather than a checkpoint capture (capture\n139|operation, record bytes, checkpoint). The two receipts are never\n140|interchangeable: different operations, different idempotency keys,\n141|different digests, different result bindings. Sharing one shape would\n142|merge the namespaces the idempotency rules keep apart.\n143|\n144|## Stated bounds\n145|\n146|- The journal and marker shapes validate in this package; the\n147|  canonicaljson owner still registers materialization-journal 2.0.0\n148|  (and materialization-plan 1.0.0) with\n149|  rejectUnsupportedImmutableObjectShape, and its census and inventory\n150|  suites pin that registration. Replacing it is outside this leaf.\n151|- The plan is an opaque digest input; only its authority routing view\n152|  (kind, platform, root path) is cross-checked. Operation-predecessor\n153|  and prior-checkpoint classification rules stay with the plan owner.\n154|- Status probes (provider, bridge, marker, lease, native) are modeled\n155|  inputs. No Mesh RPC, provider plugin, bridge process, or lease\n156|  arbitration is driven here.\n157|- Filesystem staging removal and predecessor restoration are\n158|  coordinator work; the journal records the converged states and the\n159|  probe-verified closure facts.\n160|- Marker history/current files belong to the replica owner; this\n161|  package validates marker bytes and classifies destinations.\n162|- The package adds no `ax` command, no `doctor` result, and no runtime\n163|  capability claim.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
