{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c641","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae2b-f4bb-7310-a5c5-e45123d43dca"},"sequence":379,"recorded_at":1780531400000753,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"f3ccc2af-522d-4b28-99ba-3a506c9bdcb3","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"f3ccc2af-522d-4b28-99ba-3a506c9bdcb3","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"f3ccc2af-522d-4b28-99ba-3a506c9bdcb3"},"call_id":"call_01a0ae2d3780771ebb756fc5ee1d5118","text":"Read text file `internal/matjournal/recover.go`.\n(140 line(s) above)\n141|type RecoveryInput struct {\n142|\tBoundary    string\n143|\tPath        string\n144|\tProvider    ProviderProbe\n145|\tBridge      BridgeProbe\n146|\tMarker      string\n147|\tHost        string\n148|\tLeaseKnown  bool\n149|\tLeaseBefore LeaseIdentity\n150|\tLeaseAfter  LeaseIdentity\n151|\t// NativeKnown gates the native identity/binding comparison. It is\n152|\t// required only when the journal carries a provider transaction\n153|\t// or an adopted bridge binding; otherwise no native identity\n154|\t// exists to compare.\n155|\tNativeKnown  bool\n156|\tNativeBefore string\n157|\tNativeAfter  string\n158|\t// ExternalEffect describes the possibly executed external effect\n159|\t// the probes reconcile (for example \"bridge adopt may have\n160|\t// adopted the dormant manager\").\n161|\tExternalEffect string\n162|\t// MarkerBytes carries the probe-attested destination marker for\n163|\t// a workspace commit completion; PriorMarkerBytes carries its\n164|\t// predecessor link when non-null. Both validate through the\n165|\t// closed marker shape before anything binds them.\n166|\tMarkerBytes      []byte\n167|\tPriorMarkerBytes []byte\n168|\t// PredecessorsRestored and StagingRemoved are the probe-verified\n169|\t// rollback-closure facts.\n170|\tPredecessorsRestored bool\n171|\tStagingRemoved       bool\n172|}\n173|\n174|// Evidence is the Section 13.13 conformance record for one recovery\n175|// assessment: boundary ID, path, operation IDs, pre/post durable\n176|// facts, external effect and status probe, winning lease and native\n177|// identity before/after, the selected outcome, and the reason and\n178|// remediation satisfying that outcome. Parked and rollback assessments\n179|// persist durably as recovery.json; safe_retry establishes no new\n180|// durable fact beyond the journal and receipt it returns.\n181|type Evidence struct {\n182|\tMaterializationID string            `json:\"materialization_id\"`\n183|\tBoundary          string            `json:\"boundary\"`\n184|\tPath              string            `json:\"path\"`\n185|\tOperationIDs      map[string]string `json:\"operation_ids\"`\n186|\tPhaseBefore       string            `json:\"phase_before\"`\n187|\tPhaseAfter        string            `json:\"phase_after\"`\n188|\tReceiptPresent    bool              `json:\"receipt_present\"`\n189|\tProviderState     string            `json:\"provider_state\"`\n190|\tBridgeState       string            `json:\"bridge_state\"`\n191|\tExternalEffect    string            `json:\"external_effect\"`\n192|\tStatusProbe       string            `json:\"status_probe\"`\n193|\tLeaseBefore       LeaseIdentity     `json:\"lease_before\"`\n194|\tLeaseAfter        LeaseIdentity     `json:\"lease_after\"`\n195|\tNativeBefore      string            `json:\"native_before\"`\n196|\tNativeAfter       string            `json:\"native_after\"`\n197|\tSelected          Outcome           `json:\"selected\"`\n198|\tReason            string            `json:\"reason\"`\n199|\tRemediation       string            `json:\"remediation\"`\n200|\tDecidedAt         string            `json:\"decided_at\"`\n201|}\n202|\n203|// parkedFailure builds the blocking-reason Structured Error for a\n204|// parked assessment: the named code with retryable false (parked\n205|// ambiguity is never retry permission).\n206|func parkedFailure(code axerror.Code, message string, operation string) (*axerror.Error, error) {\n207|\tids := axerror.NoIDs()\n208|\tif operation != \"\" {\n209|\t\tparsed, err := scalar.ParseUUIDv7(operation)\n210|\t\tif err == nil {\n211|\t\t\tids = ids.WithOperation(parsed)\n212|\t\t}\n213|\t}\n214|\treturn axerror.New(axerror.Spec{\n215|\t\tVersion:   lastErrorVersion,\n216|\t\tCode:      code,\n217|\t\tMessage:   message,\n218|\t\tRetryable: false,\n219|\t\tIDs:       ids,\n220|\t\tDetails:   axerror.Details{},\n221|\t})\n222|}\n223|\n224|// rollbackFailure builds the terminal-reason Structured Error for an\n225|// executed rollback.\n226|func rollbackFailure(code axerror.Code, message string, operation string) (*axerror.Error, error) {\n227|\treturn parkedFailure(code, message, operation)\n228|}\n229|\n230|// Recover classifies one crashed materialization after a clean restart\n231|// into exactly one Section 13.13 outcome. It reads durable facts first\n232|// (journal, receipt, plan view), then applies the rejection gates in\n233|// order: unknown or moved authority, substitution, two live\n234|// authorities, unfenced continuation, host conditions, marker\n235|// integrity, unknown decisive status, and contradictory probes all\n236|// park. Rollback-required facts execute the allowed abort and return\n237|// explicit_rollback; provable terminal completions (commit, dormant\n238|// finalize, rollback close) apply and return safe_retry; every other\n239|// consistent assessment resumes or replays with safe_retry.\n240|//\n241|// Parked assessments record the blocking reason as last_error (except\n242|// on a terminal journal, which stays frozen) and persist the evidence\n243|// as recovery.json. Rollback assessments persist the terminal journal\n244|// and the evidence. Safe_retry assessments mutate nothing: the journal\n245|// and receipt they return are the evidence.\n246|func (store *Store) Recover(materializationID string, input RecoveryInput) (Outcome, Evidence, error) {\n247|\tid, err := checkUUIDv7(materializationID, \"materialization_id\")\n248|\tif err != nil {\n249|\t\treturn \"\", Evidence{}, err\n250|\t}\n251|\tif !validBoundary(input.Boundary) {\n252|\t\treturn \"\", Evidence{}, invalid(\"recovery boundary %q is outside CR-MAT-01..08\", input.Boundary)\n253|\t}\n254|\tif !validPath(input.Path) {\n255|\t\treturn \"\", Evidence{}, invalid(\"recovery path %q is outside the CR-MAT path set\", input.Path)\n256|\t}\n257|\tif err := checkRecoveryProbes(&input); err != nil {\n258|\t\treturn \"\", Evidence{}, err\n259|\t}\n260|\tstore.mutex.Lock()\n261|\tdefer store.mutex.Unlock()\n262|\tmatDir := filepath.Join(store.root, id)\n263|\traw, err := readJournalFile(filepath.Join(matDir, \"journal.json\"))\n264|\tif err != nil {\n265|\t\tif os.IsNotExist(err) {\n266|\t\t\tif input.Boundary != BoundaryBeforeCreate {\n267|\t\t\t\treturn \"\", Evidence{}, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: %s\", ErrUnknownJournal, id)\n268|\t\t\t}\n269|\t\t\treturn store.recoverBeforeCreateLocked(id, input)\n270|\t\t}\n271|\t\treturn \"\", Evidence{}, err\n272|\t}\n273|\tview, err := store.readPlanViewLocked(matDir)\n274|\tif err != nil {\n275|\t\treturn \"\", Evidence{}, err\n276|\t}\n277|\tjournal, err := decodeJournal(raw, view)\n278|\tif err != nil {\n279|\t\treturn store.parkTornLocked(id, matDir, input, err)\n280|\t}\n281|\t_, receiptPresent, err := store.readReceiptLocked(matDir, journal.PrepareOperationID)\n282|\tif err != nil {\n283|\t\treturn \"\", Evidence{}, err\n284|\t}\n285|\tassessment := recoveryAssessment{\n286|\t\tstore:          store,\n287|\t\tmatDir:         matDir,\n288|\t\tjournal:        &journal,\n289|\t\tview:           view,\n290|\t\tinput:          input,\n291|\t\treceiptPresent: receiptPresent,\n292|\t}\n293|\treturn assessment.decide()\n294|}\n295|\n296|// checkRecoveryProbes validates the modeled probe enums and the lease\n297|// observations.\n298|func checkRecoveryProbes(input *RecoveryInput) error {\n299|\tswitch input.Provider.State {\n300|\tcase ProviderUnknown, ProviderPrepared, ProviderCommitted, ProviderRolledBack:\n301|\tdefault:\n302|\t\treturn invalid(\"provider probe state %q is outside the closed enum\", input.Provider.State)\n303|\t}\n304|\tswitch input.Bridge.State {\n305|\tcase ProviderUnknown, BoardNotStarted, BoardImported, BoardOpened, BoardAdopted,\n306|\t\tBoardResumed, BoardDormantFinalized, BoardRolledBack, BoardFailed,\n307|\t\t\"dormant\", \"quiesced\", \"stopped\", \"running\", \"idle\":\n308|\tdefault:\n309|\t\treturn invalid(\"bridge probe state %q is outside the closed vocabulary\", input.Bridge.State)\n310|\t}\n311|\tswitch input.Marker {\n312|\tcase MarkerAbsent, MarkerValidMatch, MarkerMismatch, MarkerInvalid:\n313|\tdefault:\n314|\t\treturn invalid(\"marker probe %q is outside the closed vocabulary\", input.Marker)\n315|\t}\n316|\tswitch input.Host {\n317|\tcase HostOK, HostDiskFull, HostRenameBlocked:\n318|\tdefault:\n319|\t\treturn invalid(\"host condition %q is outside the closed vocabulary\", input.Host)\n320|\t}\n321|\tif input.LeaseKnown {\n322|\t\tif input.LeaseBefore.Epoch < 1 || input.LeaseBefore.Epoch > uint53Max {\n323|\t\t\treturn invalid(\"recovery winning lease epoch %d is outside 1..2^53-1\", input.LeaseBefore.Epoch)\n324|\t\t}\n325|\t\tif _, err := scalar.ParseUUIDv4(input.LeaseBefore.ID); err != nil {\n326|\t\t\treturn invalid(\"recovery winning lease id: %v\", err)\n327|\t\t}\n328|\t\tif input.LeaseAfter.Epoch < 1 || input.LeaseAfter.Epoch > uint53Max {\n329|\t\t\treturn invalid(\"recovery winning lease epoch %d is outside 1..2^53-1\", input.LeaseAfter.Epoch)\n330|\t\t}\n331|\t\tif _, err := scalar.ParseUUIDv4(input.LeaseAfter.ID); err != nil {\n332|\t\t\treturn invalid(\"recovery winning lease id: %v\", err)\n333|\t\t}\n334|\t}\n335|\treturn nil\n336|}\n337|\n338|// recoverBeforeCreateLocked classifies CR-MAT-01 with no journal:\n339|// nothing durable exists, so the same IDs retry fresh.\n340|func (store *Store) recoverBeforeCreateLocked(id string, input RecoveryInput) (Outcome, Evidence, error) {\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c643","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae2b-f4bb-7310-a5c5-e45123d43dca"},"sequence":380,"recorded_at":1780531400000755,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"f3ccc2af-522d-4b28-99ba-3a506c9bdcb3","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"f3ccc2af-522d-4b28-99ba-3a506c9bdcb3","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"f3ccc2af-522d-4b28-99ba-3a506c9bdcb3"},"call_id":"call_01a0ae2d3a50704c8751849aa4bc25b6","text":"Read text file `internal/matjournal/crash_unix_test.go`.\n1|//go:build darwin || linux\n2|\n3|package matjournal\n4|\n5|import (\n6|\t\"context\"\n7|\t\"errors\"\n8|\t\"os\"\n9|\t\"os/exec\"\n10|\t\"syscall\"\n11|\t\"testing\"\n12|\t\"time\"\n13|)\n14|\n15|// Real process-termination evidence for the CR-MAT-02 boundary: the\n16|// child runs the genuine production Create entry and SIGKILLs itself\n17|// between the journal install and the prepare receipt. The parent then\n18|// proves the interrupted prepare left one complete journal with no\n19|// receipt behind, and the identical retry converges with its receipt\n20|// and a safe_retry classification.\n21|//\n22|// The child rebuilds nothing: it opens the parent's data directory\n23|// from the environment, so its closure inputs are byte-identical to\n24|// the parent's retry by construction.\n25|const (\n26|\tcrashChildEnv   = \"AX_MATJOURNAL_CRASH_CHILD\"\n27|\tcrashChildStore = \"AX_MATJOURNAL_CRASH_STORE\"\n28|)\n29|\n30|func TestCreateCrashChildSelfTerminates(t *testing.T) {\n31|\tif os.Getenv(crashChildEnv) == \"1\" {\n32|\t\tcreateCrashChild()\n33|\t\treturn\n34|\t}\n35|\tstoreDir := t.TempDir()\n36|\tif _, err := Open(storeDir); err != nil {\n37|\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n38|\t}\n39|\t// A bounded context keeps a hung child a test failure,\n40|\t// never a hung suite: the child must die at the boundary or\n41|\t// not return at all.\n42|\tctx, cancel := context.WithTimeout(context.Background(), 60*time.Second)\n43|\tdefer cancel()\n44|\tchild := exec.CommandContext(ctx, os.Args[0],\n45|\t\t\"-test.run=^TestCreateCrashChildSelfTerminates$\",\n46|\t\t\"-test.count=1\",\n47|\t)\n48|\tchild.Env = append(os.Environ(),\n49|\t\tcrashChildEnv+\"=1\",\n50|\t\tcrashChildStore+\"=\"+storeDir,\n51|\t)\n52|\trunErr := child.Run()\n53|\tvar exitErr *exec.ExitError\n54|\tif !errors.As(runErr, &exitErr) {\n55|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"child run = %v, want a signal-kill exit\", runErr)\n56|\t}\n57|\tstatus, ok := exitErr.Sys().(syscall.WaitStatus)\n58|\tif !ok || !status.Signaled() || status.Signal() != syscall.SIGKILL {\n59|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"child status = %v, want killed by SIGKILL\", exitErr)\n60|\t}\n61|\t// The kill landed between the journal and the receipt: one\n62|\t// complete journal that verifies, no receipt, no partial bytes.\n63|\tparent, err := Open(storeDir)\n64|\tif err != nil {\n65|\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n66|\t}\n67|\tparent.Now = fixedClock\n68|\tif journal, receipt := journalFilesExist(t, parent); !journal || receipt {\n69|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"after SIGKILL: journal = %v, receipt = %v, want true, false\", journal, receipt)\n70|\t}\n71|\tloaded, _, err := parent.Get(testMatID)\n72|\tif err != nil {\n73|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"Get after SIGKILL error = %v\", err)\n74|\t}\n75|\tif loaded.Phase != PhaseStaging {\n76|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"phase = %q\", loaded.Phase)\n77|\t}\n78|\t// The identical retry converges on the recorded journal with\n79|\t// its receipt: the interrupted prepare is resumed, not\n80|\t// duplicated. Recovery then classifies safe_retry.\n81|\tref, _ := mustCreate(t, parent, testInputsComposite())\n82|\tif ref.PrepareOperationID != testPrepareOp {\n83|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"retry PrepareOperationID = %q\", ref.PrepareOperationID)\n84|\t}\n85|\tif journal, receipt := journalFilesExist(t, parent); !journal || !receipt {\n86|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"after retry: journal = %v, receipt = %v, want true, true\", journal, receipt)\n87|\t}\n88|\tinput := baseRecoveryInput()\n89|\tinput.Boundary = BoundaryAfterPrepare\n90|\toutcome, _, err := parent.Recover(testMatID, input)\n91|\tif err != nil {\n92|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"Recover error = %v\", err)\n93|\t}\n94|\tmustOutcome(t, outcome, OutcomeSafeRetry, \"Recover(CR-MAT-02 SIGKILL)\")\n95|}\n96|\n97|// createCrashChild runs the production Create entry and kills its own\n98|// process at the AfterJournal boundary. It never returns.\n99|func createCrashChild() {\n100|\tstore, err := Open(os.Getenv(crashChildStore))\n101|\tif err != nil {\n102|\t\tos.Exit(66)\n103|\t}\n104|\tstore.AfterJournal = func() error {\n105|\t\t_ = syscall.Kill(syscall.Getpid(), syscall.SIGKILL)\n106|\t\t// The kill is asynchronous under instrumentation: block\n107|\t\t// here so a delivered SIGKILL always wins the race\n108|\t\t// against process exit. If the kill failed, the parent\n109|\t\t// context times out and fails the test instead of\n110|\t\t// passing on a wrong exit.\n111|\t\tselect {}\n112|\t}\n113|\t_, _, _ = store.Create(testInputsComposite())\n114|\t// The hook must have fired: reaching here means the boundary\n115|\t// was skipped, so fail the parent with a clean exit.\n116|\tos.Exit(0)\n117|}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c645","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae2b-f4bb-7310-a5c5-e45123d43dca"},"sequence":381,"recorded_at":1780531400000757,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"f3ccc2af-522d-4b28-99ba-3a506c9bdcb3","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"f3ccc2af-522d-4b28-99ba-3a506c9bdcb3","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"f3ccc2af-522d-4b28-99ba-3a506c9bdcb3"},"call_id":"call_01a0ae2d3bcd71b09f489db2a0862ee2","text":"Read text file `internal/sessckpt/crash_unix_test.go`.\n1|//go:build darwin || linux\n2|\n3|package sessckpt\n4|\n5|import (\n6|\t\"context\"\n7|\t\"errors\"\n8|\t\"os\"\n9|\t\"os/exec\"\n10|\t\"syscall\"\n11|\t\"testing\"\n12|\t\"time\"\n13|\n14|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/sessrepo\"\n15|)\n16|\n17|// Real process-termination evidence for the crash boundary: the\n18|// child runs the genuine production Capture entry and SIGKILLs\n19|// itself between the checkpoint-blob install and the operation\n20|// receipt. The parent then proves the interrupted capture left no\n21|// partial record behind and the identical retry converges.\n22|//\n23|// The child rebuilds nothing: it opens the parent's repository\n24|// and store directories from the environment and derives the same\n25|// head from the chain, so its closure inputs are byte-identical\n26|// to the parent's retry by construction.\n27|const (\n28|\tcrashChildEnv   = \"AX_SESSCKPT_CRASH_CHILD\"\n29|\tcrashChildRepo  = \"AX_SESSCKPT_CRASH_REPO\"\n30|\tcrashChildStore = \"AX_SESSCKPT_CRASH_STORE\"\n31|)\n32|\n33|func TestCaptureCrashChildSelfTerminates(t *testing.T) {\n34|\tif os.Getenv(crashChildEnv) == \"1\" {\n35|\t\tcaptureCrashChild()\n36|\t\treturn\n37|\t}\n38|\trepoDir := t.TempDir()\n39|\trepo, err := sessrepo.Open(repoDir)\n40|\tif err != nil {\n41|\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n42|\t}\n43|\trecord := decodeObject(t, specSessionRecord)\n44|\trecord[\"session_id\"], record[\"subject_id\"], record[\"name\"] = testSessionID, testSessionID, \"alpha\"\n45|\tidentified := identify(t, record, \"record_id\")\n46|\tref, err := repo.CreateSession(identified)\n47|\tif err != nil {\n48|\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n49|\t}\n50|\t_ = appendChainEvent(t, repo, \"session.created\", 1, testLease, 1, ref.RecordID, map[string]any{\n51|\t\t\"session_record_id\": ref.RecordID, \"bootstrap_operation_id\": testHostA, \"first_checkpoint_operation_id\": testHostB,\n52|\t})\n53|\tstoreDir := t.TempDir()\n54|\tif _, err := Open(storeDir); err != nil {\n55|\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n56|\t}\n57|\t// A bounded context keeps a hung child a test failure,\n58|\t// never a hung suite: the child must die at the boundary or\n59|\t// not return at all.\n60|\tctx, cancel := context.WithTimeout(context.Background(), 60*time.Second)\n61|\tdefer cancel()\n62|\tchild := exec.CommandContext(ctx, os.Args[0],\n63|\t\t\"-test.run=^TestCaptureCrashChildSelfTerminates$\",\n64|\t\t\"-test.count=1\",\n65|\t)\n66|\tchild.Env = append(os.Environ(),\n67|\t\tcrashChildEnv+\"=1\",\n68|\t\tcrashChildRepo+\"=\"+repoDir,\n69|\t\tcrashChildStore+\"=\"+storeDir,\n70|\t)\n71|\trunErr := child.Run()\n72|\tvar exitErr *exec.ExitError\n73|\tif !errors.As(runErr, &exitErr) {\n74|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"child run = %v, want a signal-kill exit\", runErr)\n75|\t}\n76|\tstatus, ok := exitErr.Sys().(syscall.WaitStatus)\n77|\tif !ok || !status.Signaled() || status.Signal() != syscall.SIGKILL {\n78|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"child status = %v, want killed by SIGKILL\", exitErr)\n79|\t}\n80|\t// The kill landed between the blob and the receipt: one\n81|\t// complete blob that verifies, no receipt, no partial bytes.\n82|\tparent, err := Open(storeDir)\n83|\tif err != nil {\n84|\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n85|\t}\n86|\tif blobs, receipts := countFiles(t, parent); blobs != 1 || receipts != 0 {\n87|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"after SIGKILL: blobs = %d, receipts = %d, want 1, 0\", blobs, receipts)\n88|\t}\n89|\teveryFileVerifies(t, parent)\n90|\t// The identical retry converges on one checkpoint identity\n91|\t// with its receipt: the interrupted capture is resumed, not\n92|\t// duplicated.\n93|\tchain, err := sessrepo.Open(repoDir)\n94|\tif err != nil {\n95|\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n96|\t}\n97|\tevents, err := chain.ListEvents(testSessionID)\n98|\tif err != nil {\n99|\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n100|\t}\n101|\tif len(events) != 1 {\n102|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"chain events = %d, want the single bootstrap event\", len(events))\n103|\t}\n104|\trecovered, raw, err := parent.Capture(chain, testInputs([]string{events[0].EventID}, testOpA))\n105|\tif err != nil {\n106|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"retry Capture error = %v\", err)\n107|\t}\n108|\tif recovered.OperationID != testOpA {\n109|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"retry OperationID = %q\", recovered.OperationID)\n110|\t}\n111|\tstored, err := parent.Get(recovered.CheckpointID)\n112|\tif err != nil {\n113|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"Get after retry error = %v\", err)\n114|\t}\n115|\tif string(stored) != string(raw) {\n116|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"retry bytes differ from stored bytes\")\n117|\t}\n118|\tif blobs, receipts := countFiles(t, parent); blobs != 1 || receipts != 1 {\n119|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"after retry: blobs = %d, receipts = %d, want 1, 1\", blobs, receipts)\n120|\t}\n121|}\n122|\n123|// captureCrashChild runs the production Capture entry and kills\n124|// its own process at the AfterBlob boundary. It never returns.\n125|func captureCrashChild() {\n126|\trepo, err := sessrepo.Open(os.Getenv(crashChildRepo))\n127|\tif err != nil {\n128|\t\tos.Exit(64)\n129|\t}\n130|\tevents, err := repo.ListEvents(testSessionID)\n131|\tif err != nil || len(events) != 1 {\n132|\t\tos.Exit(65)\n133|\t}\n134|\tstore, err := Open(os.Getenv(crashChildStore))\n135|\tif err != nil {\n136|\t\tos.Exit(66)\n137|\t}\n138|\tstore.AfterBlob = func() error {\n139|\t\t_ = syscall.Kill(syscall.Getpid(), syscall.SIGKILL)\n140|\t\t// The kill is asynchronous under instrumentation: block\n141|\t\t// here so a delivered SIGKILL always wins the race\n142|\t\t// against process exit. If the kill failed, the parent\n143|\t\t// context times out and fails the test instead of\n144|\t\t// passing on a wrong exit.\n145|\t\tselect {}\n146|\t}\n147|\t_, _, _ = store.Capture(repo, testInputs([]string{events[0].EventID}, testOpA))\n148|\t// The hook must have fired: reaching here means the boundary\n149|\t// was skipped, so fail the parent with a clean exit.\n150|\tos.Exit(0)\n151|}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
