{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c779","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae2b-f4bb-7310-a5c5-e45123d43dca"},"sequence":535,"recorded_at":1780531400001065,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"f3ccc2af-522d-4b28-99ba-3a506c9bdcb3","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"f3ccc2af-522d-4b28-99ba-3a506c9bdcb3","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"f3ccc2af-522d-4b28-99ba-3a506c9bdcb3"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ae2d-a2ec-7820-9937-c5a3e2962517"},"task_id":"01a0ae2d-a2ec-7820-9937-c5a3e2962517","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0ae2d-a2ec-7820-9937-c5a3e2962517","chunk":"Read text file `README.md`.\n(1959 line(s) above)\n1960|`TestRev12ReferencedCheckpointLaterLease`,\n1961|`TestRev11RecordConsumptionCensus`,\n1962|`TestRev12RecordConsumptionCensusRejectsAlternatePaths`, and\n1963|`TestRev12AdmissionPrecisionCensus`, `TestRev14CapabilitySeal`, and\n1964|`TestRev14RecordConsumptionCensusRejectsAlternatePaths`, and\n1965|`TestRev15AliasAwareRecordConsumptionCensus` in the shared `sessquery`\n1966|package. The rev16 mutation run records 66 applied N/B plants (63\n1967|narrowing, 3 ordering), all killed, plus separate classifier controls;\n1968|it proves exact callback provenance and normalizes Go aliases across\n1969|chained, container, function-signature, generic, interface, reflect,\n1970|and unsafe seal/token paths. Its evidence directory is attached to the\n1971|task board.\n1972|\n1973|## Workspace Checkpoint Records\n1974|\n1975|[`internal/sessckpt`](internal/sessckpt) durably installs Section 5.4\n1976|workspace checkpoint records with attested canonical identities,\n1977|idempotent capture replays, and head-bound admission against the owning\n1978|repository chain. Capture refuses malformed closures, lease-fenced\n1979|heads, and byte-unequal retries; admission refuses forged raw records,\n1980|including a same-epoch foreign-lease head. Crash seams between the blob\n1981|and the receipt replay through the recorded result, and a real SIGKILL\n1982|run proves the interrupted capture converges. The conformance matrix in\n1983|[`internal/sessckpt/TRACEABILITY.md`](internal/sessckpt/TRACEABILITY.md)\n1984|maps every clause to its production entry and test. It adds no `ax`\n1985|command, no `doctor` result, and no runtime capability claim.\n1986|\n1987|```bash\n1988|go test ./internal/sessckpt -count=1\n1989|go test ./internal/sessckpt -count=1 -cover\n1990|python3 internal/sessckpt/mutant_harness.py\n1991|```\n1992|\n1993|## Materialization Journal and Recovery\n1994|\n1995|[`internal/matjournal`](internal/matjournal) durably persists the\n1996|Section 10.6 Materialization Journal 2.0.0: the prepare-bound IDs and\n1997|canonical request digest, the phase machine with its token, bridge,\n1998|and authority rules, the no-replace prepare receipt, and the\n1999|status-first recovery evaluator that classifies every CR-MAT-01..08\n2000|boundary into exactly one Section 13.13 outcome with parked and\n2001|rollback evidence. Recovery executes allowed aborts and provable\n2002|terminal completions, records parked assessments with the retained\n2003|lease, exact IDs, and blocking reason, and never invents a fourth\n2004|outcome. Provider, bridge, marker, lease, and native states arrive as\n2005|modeled status inputs; the package drives no process and claims no\n2006|peer behavior. The conformance matrix in\n2007|[`internal/matjournal/TRACEABILITY.md`](internal/matjournal/TRACEABILITY.md)\n2008|maps every clause to its production entry, test, and narrowing mutant.\n2009|It adds no `ax` command, no `doctor` result, and no runtime capability\n2010|claim.\n2011|\n2012|```bash\n2013|go test ./internal/matjournal -count=1\n2014|go test ./internal/matjournal -count=1 -cover\n2015|python3 internal/matjournal/mutant_harness.py\n2016|```\n2017|\n2018|## Structured Errors, Stable Codes, and Causal Redaction\n2019|\n2020|[`internal/axerror`](internal/axerror) implements the Section 15 Structured\n2021|Error contract: the closed versioned failure object, its stable code-to-exit\n2022|registry, its retryability rule, its typed diagnostic details, and the redaction\n2023|that keeps a local cause off the wire. The package holds no state, opens no\n2024|file, starts no process, and mutates nothing durable, so it has no crash or\n2025|idempotency surface and advertises no provider, platform, backend, or CLI\n2026|capability.\n2027|\n2028|| Element | Where it is decided |\n2029|| --- | --- |\n2030|| Versions `1.0.0`, `1.1.0`, `1.2.0`, `1.3.0` | `Version` constants; any other value, including major 2, is refused rather than coerced |\n2031|| Code-to-exit registry | `ExitCodeFor`, projected from the reviewed catalog rather than retyped, and admitting a code only for the versions that register it |\n2032|| Exit-status registry | `ExitStatusMeaning` and `IsFailureExitStatus`, the closed Section 15.2 table, whose eighteen rows are measured from [`internal/specdoc`](internal/specdoc) rather than restated in prose; success is never a failure class |\n2033|| Containing-contract binding | `BindingFor`, a static table with no negotiation path; `DecodeBound` takes the version from the container, never from the payload |\n2034|| Retryability | `RetryabilityRefusal`, quoting the clause that disqualifies each exit class and each individually named code |\n2035|| Typed details | `TargetAuth` and `RealmEvidence`, plus a presence requirement on `target_auth_missing` that the generic constructor cannot bypass |\n2036|| Redaction | `ValidateDetails` exact-key scanner over the four Section 15.1 detail classes, and `refuseCausalLeak` over the local cause chain |\n2037|| Detail ownership | `New` deep-copies the caller's diagnostic graph and `Detail` deep-copies on the way out, so the graph `ValidateDetails` checked is the graph the object encodes |\n2038|| Untrusted boundaries | `LocalFromUntrusted`, which takes no part of a child or peer payload |\n2039|\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
