{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c8c1","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae2b-f4bb-7310-a5c5-e45123d43dca"},"sequence":699,"recorded_at":1780531400001393,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"f3ccc2af-522d-4b28-99ba-3a506c9bdcb3","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"f3ccc2af-522d-4b28-99ba-3a506c9bdcb3","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"f3ccc2af-522d-4b28-99ba-3a506c9bdcb3"},"call_id":"call_01a0ae2f7e2b73c28dab0265488edd1a","text":"Read text file `internal/matjournal/store.go`.\n1|package matjournal\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"bytes\"\n5|\t\"encoding/json\"\n6|\t\"fmt\"\n7|\t\"os\"\n8|\t\"path/filepath\"\n9|\t\"runtime\"\n10|\t\"sort\"\n11|\t\"sync\"\n12|\t\"time\"\n13|\n14|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/axerror\"\n15|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/canonicaljson\"\n16|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/environ\"\n17|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/scalar\"\n18|)\n19|\n20|// Store durably installs Materialization Journals with their plan\n21|// routing views and prepare receipts under one data root. Journals are\n22|// mutable: creation installs no-replace, and every later phase or\n23|// sub-state move replaces atomically, so a crash leaves either nothing\n24|// or complete re-validating bytes.\n25|//\n26|// BeforeWrite fires after validation and before the first durable byte\n27|// of an operation; AfterJournal fires after each durable journal write\n28|// inside the operation; AfterCommit fires after the operation's last\n29|// durable write. All three are nil in normal operation. Tests connect\n30|// them to a secconftest Injector firing the owner's own points (a fault\n31|// before any durable byte carries safe_retry) or to plain faults for\n32|// the interior seams.\n33|type Store struct {\n34|\troot         string\n35|\tmutex        sync.Mutex\n36|\tBeforeWrite  func() error\n37|\tAfterJournal func() error\n38|\tAfterCommit  func() error\n39|\t// Now reports the instant stamped as started_at/updated_at. Nil\n40|\t// reads the wall clock in UTC; tests inject a fixed clock.\n41|\tNow func() time.Time\n42|}\n43|\n44|// Open binds a journal store to the materializations namespace beneath\n45|// dataRoot, creating it owner-only when absent. The root must be\n46|// absolute.\n47|func Open(dataRoot string) (*Store, error) {\n48|\tif !filepath.IsAbs(dataRoot) {\n49|\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: data root %q is not absolute\", ErrInvalidJournal, dataRoot)\n50|\t}\n51|\troot := filepath.Join(dataRoot, \"materializations\")\n52|\tif err := os.MkdirAll(root, 0o700); err != nil {\n53|\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"create materializations root %q: %w\", root, err)\n54|\t}\n55|\treturn &Store{root: root}, nil\n56|}\n57|\n58|// JournalRef names one durable journal: its materialization identity\n59|// with the prepare operation that created it and its current phase.\n60|type JournalRef struct {\n61|\tMaterializationID  string\n62|\tPrepareOperationID string\n63|\tPhase              string\n64|}\n65|\n66|// TransitionOpts carries phase-entry evidence: the destination marker\n67|// (with its prior chain link) for a workspace commit, and the\n68|// explaining Structured Error for a failure.\n69|type TransitionOpts struct {\n70|\tMarker      []byte\n71|\tPriorMarker []byte\n72|\tLastError   json.RawMessage\n73|}\n74|\n75|// prepareReceipt is the machine-local prepare record: the caller-stable\n76|// prepare identity with the journal it created and the canonical\n77|// request bytes that make a retry comparable. It adopts the sessckpt\n78|// operation-receipt discipline (operation key, input digest, no-replace\n79|// install after the bytes it names) and is a distinct record because\n80|// it binds the materialize.prepare namespace rather than a checkpoint\n81|// capture; see TRACEABILITY.md.\n82|type prepareReceipt struct {\n83|\tOperationID       string `json:\"operation_id\"`\n84|\tMaterializationID string `json:\"materialization_id\"`\n85|\tInputDigest       string `json:\"input_digest\"`\n86|\tCanonicalRequest  string `json:\"canonical_request\"`\n87|\tPhase             string `json:\"phase\"`\n88|}\n89|\n90|func (store *Store) now() string {\n91|\tnow := time.Now().UTC()\n92|\tif store.Now != nil {\n93|\t\tnow = store.Now().UTC()\n94|\t}\n95|\treturn now.Format(\"2006-01-02T15:04:05.000Z07:00\")\n96|}\n97|\n98|// Create binds the prepare closure durably: both caller-stable IDs and\n99|// the canonical request digest install before any staging authority or\n100|// bridge mutation. The same IDs retried with a byte-identical body\n101|// replay the recorded journal without writing; the same IDs retried\n102|// with a moved body refuse ErrJournalConflict and write nothing.\n103|func (store *Store) Create(inputs CreateInputs) (JournalRef, []byte, error) {\n104|\tstarted, err := checkTimestamp(store.now(), \"started_at\")\n105|\tif err != nil {\n106|\t\treturn JournalRef{}, nil, err\n107|\t}\n108|\tjournal, view, digest, err := buildCreate(inputs, started)\n109|\tif err != nil {\n110|\t\treturn JournalRef{}, nil, err\n111|\t}\n112|\tcanonical, err := canonicalRequestBody(inputs.RequestBody)\n113|\tif err != nil {\n114|\t\treturn JournalRef{}, nil, err\n115|\t}\n116|\tstore.mutex.Lock()\n117|\tdefer store.mutex.Unlock()\n118|\tif recorded, raw, ok, err := store.replayCreateLocked(journal.MaterializationID, journal.PrepareOperationID, digest, canonical); err != nil {\n119|\t\treturn JournalRef{}, nil, err\n120|\t} else if ok {\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c8c3","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae2b-f4bb-7310-a5c5-e45123d43dca"},"sequence":700,"recorded_at":1780531400001395,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"f3ccc2af-522d-4b28-99ba-3a506c9bdcb3","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"f3ccc2af-522d-4b28-99ba-3a506c9bdcb3","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"f3ccc2af-522d-4b28-99ba-3a506c9bdcb3"},"call_id":"call_01a0ae2f804a7181871ec48e153fbe6e","text":"Read text file `internal/sessckpt/store.go`.\n1|package sessckpt\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"errors\"\n5|\t\"fmt\"\n6|\t\"os\"\n7|\t\"path/filepath\"\n8|\t\"runtime\"\n9|\t\"sync\"\n10|\n11|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/scalar\"\n12|)\n13|\n14|// ErrInvalidCheckpoint reports a checkpoint closure that must be\n15|// refused before publication. It always wraps\n16|// canonicaljson.ErrInvalidIdentity, so errors.Is proves the SPEC\n17|// Section 5.4 incompatible_schema class for every unpublishable\n18|// closure, including the CP-N1..CP-N4 fixtures.\n19|var ErrInvalidCheckpoint = errors.New(\"invalid checkpoint closure\")\n20|\n21|// ErrCheckpointConflict reports the idempotency boundary: the same\n22|// capture operation retried with moved inputs\n23|// (idempotency_mismatch), or a digest path holding bytes that\n24|// disagree with the installing candidate (a torn store, never a\n25|// second version of an immutable record).\n26|var ErrCheckpointConflict = errors.New(\"checkpoint capture conflict\")\n27|\n28|// Store durably installs Checkpoint Records and their operation\n29|// receipts under one data root. Checkpoint blobs are\n30|// content-addressed and installed no-replace, so capture is\n31|// append-only by construction and there is no update or delete\n32|// entry to test.\n33|//\n34|// BeforeWrite fires after validation and before the first durable\n35|// byte; AfterBlob fires after the checkpoint blob is durable and\n36|// before the operation receipt; AfterCommit fires after the receipt\n37|// is durable. All three are nil in normal operation. Tests connect\n38|// them to a secconftest Injector firing the owner's own points: a\n39|// fault before any durable byte carries safe_retry, a fault past\n40|// any durable step carries recoverable_parked_state until the\n41|// identical retry replays the recorded result, and a fault past\n42|// the receipt carries safe_retry through the replayed receipt.\n43|type Store struct {\n44|\troot        string\n45|\tmutex       sync.Mutex\n46|\tBeforeWrite func() error\n47|\tAfterBlob   func() error\n48|\tAfterCommit func() error\n49|}\n50|\n51|// Open binds a checkpoint store to the checkpoints namespace beneath\n52|// dataRoot, creating it owner-only when absent. The root must be\n53|// absolute.\n54|func Open(dataRoot string) (*Store, error) {\n55|\tif !filepath.IsAbs(dataRoot) {\n56|\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: data root %q is not absolute\", ErrInvalidCheckpoint, dataRoot)\n57|\t}\n58|\troot := filepath.Join(dataRoot, \"checkpoints\")\n59|\tif err := os.MkdirAll(root, 0o700); err != nil {\n60|\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"create checkpoints root %q: %w\", root, err)\n61|\t}\n62|\t// The operations namespace shares the root so one data-root\n63|\t// fsync discipline covers blobs and receipts together.\n64|\tif err := os.MkdirAll(filepath.Join(root, \"operations\"), 0o700); err != nil {\n65|\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"create checkpoint operations root: %w\", err)\n66|\t}\n67|\treturn &Store{root: root}, nil\n68|}\n69|\n70|// CheckpointRef names one durably installed Checkpoint Record: its\n71|// canonical digest and the operation receipt that installed it.\n72|type CheckpointRef struct {\n73|\tCheckpointID string\n74|\tOperationID  string\n75|}\n76|\n77|// checkpointFileName maps a validated checkpoint digest to its blob\n78|// file name. The digest passed scalar grammar before install;\n79|// invalid input maps to a sentinel name that can never collide\n80|// with a real blob.\n81|func checkpointFileName(checkpointID string) string {\n82|\tdigest, err := scalar.ParseDigest(checkpointID)\n83|\tif err != nil {\n84|\t\treturn \"invalid.json\"\n85|\t}\n86|\treturn digest.Hex() + \".json\"\n87|}\n88|\n89|// operationFileName maps a validated operation UUID to its receipt\n90|// file name. UUIDv7 grammar keeps the file name an exact,\n91|// case-stable rendering of the operation identity.\n92|func operationFileName(operationID string) string {\n93|\tid, err := scalar.ParseUUIDv7(operationID)\n94|\tif err != nil {\n95|\t\treturn \"invalid.json\"\n96|\t}\n97|\treturn id.String() + \".json\"\n98|}\n99|\n100|// installBlob installs one content-addressed blob idempotently\n101|// through the no-replace open first: a fresh path is created\n102|// atomically, and only an EEXIST loser falls back to comparing\n103|// against the winner's bytes — identical bytes are reused,\n104|// disagreeing bytes report the torn store for refusal. Leading\n105|// with the exclusive create (instead of stat-then-act) keeps the\n106|// no-replace property a filesystem fact under a second process,\n107|// not a check-then-act race the store mutex cannot see: the mutex\n108|// serializes one process, while O_EXCL serializes all of them.\n109|func installBlob(path string, data []byte) error {\n110|\tif err := writeExclusive(path, data); err == nil {\n111|\t\treturn syncDirectory(filepath.Dir(path))\n112|\t} else if !os.IsExist(err) {\n113|\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"install checkpoint blob: %w\", err)\n114|\t}\n115|\texisting, readErr := os.ReadFile(path)\n116|\tif readErr != nil {\n117|\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"read checkpoint blob for compare: %w\", readErr)\n118|\t}\n119|\tif string(existing) != string(data) {\n120|\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"%w: digest path holds disagreeing bytes\", ErrCheckpointConflict)\n121|\t}\n122|\treturn nil\n123|}\n124|\n125|// writeExclusive installs bytes at a path that must not exist. The\n126|// no-replace open makes append-only a filesystem property, not a\n127|// convention. Bytes fsync before close so a crash never leaves a\n128|// torn prefix behind.\n129|func writeExclusive(path string, data []byte) error {\n130|\tfile, err := os.OpenFile(path, os.O_WRONLY|os.O_CREATE|os.O_EXCL, 0o600)\n131|\tif err != nil {\n132|\t\treturn err\n133|\t}\n134|\tif _, err := file.Write(data); err != nil {\n135|\t\t_ = file.Close()\n136|\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"write exclusive file: %w\", err)\n137|\t}\n138|\tif err := file.Sync(); err != nil {\n139|\t\t_ = file.Close()\n140|\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"fsync exclusive file: %w\", err)\n141|\t}\n142|\tif err := file.Close(); err != nil {\n143|\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"close exclusive file: %w\", err)\n144|\t}\n145|\treturn nil\n146|}\n147|\n148|// syncDirectory fsyncs a directory so an install inside it survives\n149|// a crash. Opening a directory fails on Windows, where the install\n150|// itself is the durability boundary; there the sync is skipped,\n151|// never faked.\n152|func syncDirectory(path string) error {\n153|\tif runtime.GOOS == \"windows\" {\n154|\t\treturn nil\n155|\t}\n156|\tdirectory, err := os.Open(path)\n157|\tif err != nil {\n158|\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"open directory for fsync: %w\", err)\n159|\t}\n160|\tdefer func() { _ = directory.Close() }()\n161|\tif err := directory.Sync(); err != nil {\n162|\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"fsync directory: %w\", err)\n163|\t}\n164|\treturn nil\n165|}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c8c5","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae2b-f4bb-7310-a5c5-e45123d43dca"},"sequence":701,"recorded_at":1780531400001397,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"f3ccc2af-522d-4b28-99ba-3a506c9bdcb3","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"f3ccc2af-522d-4b28-99ba-3a506c9bdcb3","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"f3ccc2af-522d-4b28-99ba-3a506c9bdcb3"},"call_id":"call_01a0ae2f81e8712685c46b0a4e2df4a3","text":"Read text file `internal/traceability/traceability.go`.\n1|// Package traceability verifies that the pinned AX specification inventory\n2|// remains bound to concrete production declarations and executable acceptance\n3|// cases. It is a read-only repository gate; it does not advertise runtime\n4|// capabilities or mutate implementation state.\n5|package traceability\n6|\n7|import (\n8|\t\"bytes\"\n9|\t\"crypto/sha256\"\n10|\t\"encoding/hex\"\n11|\t\"encoding/json\"\n12|\t\"errors\"\n13|\t\"fmt\"\n14|\t\"go/ast\"\n15|\t\"go/parser\"\n16|\t\"go/token\"\n17|\t\"io\"\n18|\t\"io/fs\"\n19|\t\"path\"\n20|\t\"regexp\"\n21|\t\"strings\"\n22|\t\"unicode\"\n23|\t\"unicode/utf8\"\n24|\n25|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/catalog\"\n26|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/cataloggen\"\n27|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/specdoc\"\n28|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/specpin\"\n29|)\n30|\n31|const (\n32|\townershipRegistryPath = \"internal/traceability/ownership.v0.6.0.json\"\n33|\tcontractLockPath      = \"internal/specpin/v0.6.0.lock.json\"\n34|\tcatalogMetadataPath   = \"internal/catalog/catalog.v0.6.0.json\"\n35|\tgeneratedCatalogPath  = \"internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go\"\n36|\n37|\townershipFormat        = \"ax-spec-to-code-ownership\"\n38|\townershipFormatVersion = 1\n39|\n40|\t// reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256 pins the semantic JSON projection. JSON\n41|\t// formatting may change, but ownership claims cannot be self-minted without\n42|\t// an explicit review of this binding.\n43|\treviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256 = \"407c4b6a4627f0b9547869e6b9a47b631a71f8016fcf6901f94678900dd2bda3\"\n44|)\n45|\n46|var ErrTraceability = errors.New(\"spec-to-code traceability check failed\")\n47|\n48|// Report contains inventory coverage only. These counts do not claim that any\n49|// runtime capability is available, enabled, or supported.\n50|type Report struct {\n51|\tContracts              int\n52|\tNormativeSections      int\n53|\tAcceptanceCases        int\n54|\tFixtures               int\n55|\tCompatibilityContracts int\n56|\tAssignedScopes         int\n57|\n58|\t// SectionBindings and the coverage counters below are a measured ratio over\n59|\t// the registered section bindings, not a prose claim. NormativeClauses is\n60|\t// the number of RFC 2119 clause lines the pinned document itself carries in\n61|\t// the bound sections; DischargedClauses is how many of those a binding\n62|\t// enumerates with a verified excerpt and an acceptance owner.\n63|\tSectionBindings     int\n64|\tFullCoverage        int\n65|\tPartialCoverage     int\n66|\tSliverCoverage      int\n67|\tUnevidencedCoverage int\n68|\tUnmeasuredCoverage  int\n69|\tUnownedSections     int\n70|\tNormativeClauses    int\n71|\tDischargedClauses   int\n72|}\n73|\n74|type ownershipKind string\n75|\n76|const (\n77|\townershipContract         ownershipKind = \"contract\"\n78|\townershipNormativeSection ownershipKind = \"normative_section\"\n79|\townershipSectionBinding   ownershipKind = \"section_binding\"\n80|\townershipFixture          ownershipKind = \"fixture\"\n81|)\n82|\n83|type ownershipRegistry struct {\n84|\tFormat          string           `json:\"format\"`\n85|\tFormatVersion   int              `json:\"format_version\"`\n86|\tSource          registrySource   `json:\"source\"`\n87|\tAcceptanceCases []acceptanceCase `json:\"acceptance_cases\"`\n88|\tOwnership       []ownershipGroup `json:\"ownership\"`\n89|\tUnownedSections []unownedSection `json:\"unowned_sections\"`\n90|}\n91|\n92|// unownedSection records a real v0.6.0 section that this repository does not\n93|// implement. It exists so an unimplemented section is disclosed by name rather\n94|// than bound to a symbol from a neighbouring package, which is what an owned\n95|// key would otherwise assert. It is a disclosure, never an exemption: a section\n96|// the generated catalog requires an owner for may not be declared here, and\n97|// assigned-scope admission refuses an unowned section and prints its gap.\n98|type unownedSection struct {\n99|\tKey      string `json:\"key\"`\n100|\tGap      string `json:\"gap\"`\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
