{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cbb7","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae2b-f4bb-7310-a5c5-e45123d43dca"},"sequence":1078,"recorded_at":1780531400002151,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"f3ccc2af-522d-4b28-99ba-3a506c9bdcb3","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"f3ccc2af-522d-4b28-99ba-3a506c9bdcb3","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"f3ccc2af-522d-4b28-99ba-3a506c9bdcb3"},"call_id":"call_01a0ae31bf9a710cbf89805fa7f7790e","text":"Read text file `internal/traceability/readme_figures_pin_test.go`.\n1|package traceability\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"os\"\n5|\t\"path/filepath\"\n6|\t\"regexp\"\n7|\t\"strconv\"\n8|\t\"strings\"\n9|\t\"testing\"\n10|)\n11|\n12|// ownershipParagraphAnchor is the README heading whose first paragraph this\n13|// test measures. It is matched exactly rather than by keyword, so renaming the\n14|// heading reddens here instead of silently exempting the paragraph from\n15|// measurement.\n16|const ownershipParagraphAnchor = \"## Specification-to-Code Ownership Gate\"\n17|\n18|// publishedFigure is one number the ownership paragraph states, located by the\n19|// noun phrase that follows it and bound to the Report field it must equal. The\n20|// phrase is the identity: a figure is proven by naming what it counts, not by\n21|// its position in the sentence, so re-ordering the clause does not silently\n22|// re-point a pin at a different number.\n23|type publishedFigure struct {\n24|\tphrase  string\n25|\tmeasure func(Report) int\n26|}\n27|\n28|// publishedOwnershipFigures enumerates every figure the paragraph states. The\n29|// unpinned-figure guard below turns a deletion from this list into a red rather\n30|// than into a quietly smaller comparison, so the list is measured, not trusted.\n31|var publishedOwnershipFigures = []publishedFigure{\n32|\t{\"current contract rows\", func(report Report) int { return report.Contracts }},\n33|\t{\"pinned or catalog-referenced normative section keys\", func(report Report) int { return report.NormativeSections }},\n34|\t{\"executable acceptance cases\", func(report Report) int { return report.AcceptanceCases }},\n35|\t{\"exact section bindings\", func(report Report) int { return report.SectionBindings }},\n36|\t{\"disclosed unowned sections\", func(report Report) int { return report.UnownedSections }},\n37|\t{\"exact fixture identities\", func(report Report) int { return report.Fixtures }},\n38|\t{\"-contract subset\", func(report Report) int { return report.CompatibilityContracts }},\n39|}\n40|\n41|// ownershipParagraph returns the paragraph under the anchor, unwrapped onto one\n42|// line, together with the README line it starts at. It refuses a target it\n43|// cannot locate rather than skipping the comparison: a paragraph that silently\n44|// fell out of the measurement is exactly how the acceptance-case figure below\n45|// drifted from 73 to 74 without anything reddening.\n46|func ownershipParagraph(t *testing.T) (string, int) {\n47|\tt.Helper()\n48|\n49|\treadme, err := os.ReadFile(filepath.Join(\"..\", \"..\", \"README.md\"))\n50|\tif err != nil {\n51|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"read README.md: %v\", err)\n52|\t}\n53|\tlines := strings.Split(string(readme), \"\\n\")\n54|\tanchor := -1\n55|\tfor index, line := range lines {\n56|\t\tif strings.TrimSpace(line) == ownershipParagraphAnchor {\n57|\t\t\tif anchor >= 0 {\n58|\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"README carries the heading %q twice, at lines %d and %d; the paragraph this test measures is ambiguous\",\n59|\t\t\t\t\townershipParagraphAnchor, anchor+1, index+1)\n60|\t\t\t}\n61|\t\t\tanchor = index\n62|\t\t}\n63|\t}\n64|\tif anchor < 0 {\n65|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"README no longer carries the heading %q\", ownershipParagraphAnchor)\n66|\t}\n67|\tstart := anchor + 1\n68|\tfor start < len(lines) && strings.TrimSpace(lines[start]) == \"\" {\n69|\t\tstart++\n70|\t}\n71|\tvar body []string\n72|\tfor index := start; index < len(lines); index++ {\n73|\t\ttext := strings.TrimSpace(lines[index])\n74|\t\tif text == \"\" {\n75|\t\t\tbreak\n76|\t\t}\n77|\t\tbody = append(body, text)\n78|\t}\n79|\tif len(body) == 0 {\n80|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"README carries no paragraph under %q\", ownershipParagraphAnchor)\n81|\t}\n82|\treturn strings.Join(body, \" \"), start + 1\n83|}\n84|\n85|// isVersionDigits reports whether the digit run beginning at offset belongs to a\n86|// dotted version or path token such as v0.5.0 or ownership.v0.5.0.json, rather\n87|// than being a figure the paragraph publishes. The rule is deliberately narrow:\n88|// only a run introduced by \"v\" or preceded by a dot that itself follows a digit\n89|// is exempt, so a published figure can never be excused as version text.\n90|func isVersionDigits(paragraph string, offset int) bool {\n91|\tif offset == 0 {\n92|\t\treturn false\n93|\t}\n94|\tswitch paragraph[offset-1] {\n95|\tcase 'v', 'V':\n96|\t\treturn true\n97|\tcase '.':\n98|\t\treturn offset >= 2 && paragraph[offset-2] >= '0' && paragraph[offset-2] <= '9'\n99|\t}\n100|\treturn false\n101|}\n102|\n103|// TestREADMEOwnershipFiguresAreDerivedFromTheMeasuredReport makes the published\n104|// ownership paragraph a measurement instead of prose beside one.\n105|//\n106|// This is the third time in this artifact that a figure published next to a\n107|// measurement drifted from it: LOGBOOK 1015 records the \"nineteen §15.2 rows\"\n108|// claim against an eighteen-row table, LOGBOOK 1157 records two of the four\n109|// published fan-in rows being wrong, and this paragraph published 73 executable\n110|// acceptance cases while the registry held 74 and tracecheck printed 74. The\n111|// tool for the class already existed - parsePublishedFanIn in\n112|// internal/axerror/exit_table_pin_test.go - and had simply never been pointed at\n113|// the neighbouring sentence.\n114|//\n115|// The fix is not to assert the corrected number somewhere else. It is to leave\n116|// no figure of the paragraph unmeasured: each is located by the phrase naming\n117|// what it counts, re-derived from VerifyRepository, and any number the paragraph\n118|// states that no pinned phrase consumed is reported as unmeasured rather than\n119|// ignored.\n120|func TestREADMEOwnershipFiguresAreDerivedFromTheMeasuredReport(t *testing.T) {\n121|\tt.Parallel()\n122|\n123|\treport, err := VerifyRepository(repositorySnapshot(t))\n124|\tif err != nil {\n125|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"VerifyRepository() error = %v\", err)\n126|\t}\n127|\tparagraph, line := ownershipParagraph(t)\n128|\n129|\tconsumed := make([]bool, len(paragraph))\n130|\tfor _, figure := range publishedOwnershipFigures {\n131|\t\tpattern := regexp.MustCompile(`([0-9]+) ?` + regexp.QuoteMeta(figure.phrase))\n132|\t\tmatches := pattern.FindAllStringSubmatchIndex(paragraph, -1)\n133|\t\tif len(matches) != 1 {\n134|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"README ownership paragraph at line %d states a figure for %q %d times, want exactly 1\",\n135|\t\t\t\tline, figure.phrase, len(matches))\n136|\t\t}\n137|\t\tdigits := paragraph[matches[0][2]:matches[0][3]]\n138|\t\tpublished, convErr := strconv.Atoi(digits)\n139|\t\tif convErr != nil {\n140|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"README ownership paragraph at line %d states a non-numeric figure %q for %q\",\n141|\t\t\t\tline, digits, figure.phrase)\n142|\t\t}\n143|\t\tif measured := figure.measure(report); published != measured {\n144|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"README ownership paragraph at line %d publishes %d %s; VerifyRepository measures %d\",\n145|\t\t\t\tline, published, strings.TrimPrefix(figure.phrase, \"-\"), measured)\n146|\t\t}\n147|\t\tfor offset := matches[0][2]; offset < matches[0][3]; offset++ {\n148|\t\t\tconsumed[offset] = true\n149|\t\t}\n150|\t}\n151|\n152|\t// Every remaining digit run must be version or path text. A figure nobody\n153|\t// pinned is reported here, so adding an unmeasured number to the paragraph -\n154|\t// or deleting a row from publishedOwnershipFigures - is a red.\n155|\tfor _, run := range regexp.MustCompile(`[0-9]+`).FindAllStringIndex(paragraph, -1) {\n156|\t\tif consumed[run[0]] || isVersionDigits(paragraph, run[0]) {\n157|\t\t\tcontinue\n158|\t\t}\n159|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"README ownership paragraph at line %d states the figure %q, which no pinned phrase measures; \"+\n160|\t\t\t\"give it a row in publishedOwnershipFigures or remove it from the paragraph\",\n161|\t\t\tline, paragraph[run[0]:run[1]])\n162|\t}\n163|}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cbb9","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae2b-f4bb-7310-a5c5-e45123d43dca"},"sequence":1079,"recorded_at":1780531400002153,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"f3ccc2af-522d-4b28-99ba-3a506c9bdcb3","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"f3ccc2af-522d-4b28-99ba-3a506c9bdcb3","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"f3ccc2af-522d-4b28-99ba-3a506c9bdcb3"},"call_id":"call_01a0ae31c116709096adf277d41a2ffa","text":"Read text file `README.md`.\n(2629 line(s) above)\n2630|Regenerate and verify the committed output with:\n2631|\n2632|```bash\n2633|go generate ./internal/catalog\n2634|go run ./internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen -metadata internal/catalog/catalog.v0.6.0.json -contracts internal/specpin/v0.6.0.lock.json -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check\n2635|go test ./internal/catalog ./internal/cataloggen ./internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen -count=1\n2636|```\n2637|\n2638|## Specification-to-Code Ownership Gate\n2639|\n2640|[`internal/traceability`](internal/traceability) provides the read-only\n2641|repository gate used by CI. Its reviewed\n2642|[`ownership.v0.6.0.json`](internal/traceability/ownership.v0.6.0.json)\n2643|registry independently enumerates implementation owners for all 63 current\n2644|contract rows, 36 pinned or catalog-referenced normative section keys, 105\n2645|executable acceptance cases, 59 exact section bindings with their declared\n2646|coverage, 12 disclosed unowned sections, and 32 exact fixture identities or\n2647|Appendix D anchors. The v0.4.3 projection is checked as an owned 55-contract subset,\n2648|and the superseded v0.5.0 registry is checked as an owned legacy projection.\n2649|The generated v0.6.0 catalog also carries the reviewed schema/version/self-field\n2650|contracts used by canonical object identity calculation; generator validation\n2651|binds each row to a pinned contract and rejects duplicate, unsupported,\n2652|malformed, or digest-drifted metadata.\n2653|\n2654|The production validator re-verifies the exact source lock and reviewed catalog\n2655|metadata, refuses stale generated output, requires every production and test\n2656|owner to resolve to a real Go declaration, and rejects gaps, duplicates,\n2657|self-minted keys, partial or malformed reads, and semantic ownership drift.\n2658|GitHub Actions invokes the gate directly before generation, tests, vet, and\n2659|build:\n2660|\n2661|```bash\n2662|go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck\n2663|go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck -section 6.2\n2664|```\n2665|\n2666|The repeated `-section` form is the Story-scope production gate. It resolves\n2667|each assigned subsection, and every heading in a same-top-level range, against\n2668|the immutable v0.5.0 inventory. Every exact `section_binding` must name its own\n2669|production declaration and executable acceptance case, and must additionally\n2670|discharge the whole section it claims. A generic top-level source pin is not a\n2671|scoped implementation owner. Malformed, nonexistent, unpinned, or otherwise\n2672|unowned assignments fail closed.\n2673|\n2674|### Declared coverage and what the gate can decide\n2675|\n2676|A binding that names a real Go declaration and a real acceptance case used to be\n2677|enough. It is not: `section:2.2` named `validateSessionRecordCommon`, which\n2678|validates one enum and a name grammar, while Section 2.2 is the twenty-two\n2679|unconditional lease and replica invariants; `section:18.4` named\n2680|`OpenProjection` while Section 18.4 is audit retention and no retention code\n2681|exists. A Story assigned either section would have found it already owned and\n2682|could have done nothing.\n2683|\n2684|Every `section_binding` now declares a `coverage` level, and the gate recomputes\n2685|that level rather than believing it. The denominator is measured from\n2686|[`internal/specdoc`](internal/specdoc): the RFC 2119 clause lines the pinned\n2687|`SPEC.md` carries under the section's own heading and its subheadings. The\n2688|numerator is the `clauses` the binding enumerates, each of which must name a\n2689|clause of that inventory, quote it verbatim beginning on the exact `SPEC.md`\n2690|line it occupies, and be discharged by an acceptance case the binding itself\n2691|owns.\n2692|\n2693|| Level | Meaning | Admitted as an assigned scope |\n2694|| --- | --- | --- |\n2695|| `full` | every normative clause of the section is enumerated and discharged | yes |\n2696|| `partial` | at least half are | no |\n2697|| `sliver` | fewer than half are | no |\n2698|| `unevidenced` | none are; the registry makes no clause-level claim | no |\n2699|| `unmeasured` | the obligation scanner finds no clause line under the section at all | no |\n2700|\n2701|`unmeasured` is the honest name for what used to be called `declarative` and\n2702|used to be admitted. The scanner matches uppercase RFC 2119 keywords, so a\n2703|section that states its obligations as a table scores zero and was read as\n2704|carrying no obligation. That is false, and the first revision of this gate\n2705|reproduced the very bug it was built to remove: `-section 15.2`, the eighteen-row\n2706|normative exit-code registry, exited 0 with nothing in the tree implementing it,\n2707|and so did `-section 7.3`, the closed Provider Manifest. Nineteen of the 157\n2708|pinned headings are in that class - 7.3, 10.8.1, 13.5, 13.12, 13.14.1-13.14.5,\n2709|14.3, 14.6, 15.2, 16.6, 16.7, 18.2, 19.4 and Appendices A, B and C - and\n2710|`TestUnmeasuredCoverageIsAScannerBlindSpotNotAnAbsenceOfObligation` measures\n2711|that every one of them has a substantive body, so not one is a heading with\n2712|nothing to discharge. Keyword absence is now a failure to measure, never a\n2713|coverage claim.\n2714|\n2715|A binding below `full` must also name its gap, `unmeasured` included, and the\n2716|gap has to name the section as a whole identifier - so a sentence about 6.55 is\n2717|not a gap about 6.5 - and name the production declaration the binding is\n2718|registered to. `unowned_sections` records a section this repository does not\n2719|implement at all, with a gap and the evidence for it; an unowned entry may not\n2720|cover a section the generated catalog requires an owner for, so it is a\n2721|disclosure and never an exemption. Every one of these fields is inside the\n2722|reviewed projection digest, so none of them can be self-minted.\n2723|\n2724|This is what the gate decides, and it is less than semantic coverage. It decides\n2725|that a claimed clause is a real obligation of the claimed section, that it is\n2726|quoted verbatim at the line it occupies, that the discharging acceptance case is\n2727|registered and owned by the binding, and that the declared level equals the\n2728|measured ratio. **It cannot decide that the named acceptance case exercises the\n2729|clause's meaning.** A binding could enumerate every clause of a section and\n2730|point all of them at one weak test, and the gate would admit it. That residual\n2731|class - a complete enumeration discharged by inadequate tests - is not covered\n2732|here and is not claimed to be.\n2733|\n2734|It also cannot see an obligation stated without an RFC 2119 keyword, which is\n2735|why `unmeasured` is refused rather than admitted: the gate reports that it could\n2736|not measure the section instead of inferring that there was nothing to measure.\n2737|And the gap-quality check is a tightening rather than a proof - a sentence that\n2738|names both its section and its production declaration and still says nothing\n2739|useful is admitted, and the gate cannot decide otherwise.\n2740|\n2741|### Measured coverage of this repository\n2742|\n2743|`tracecheck` prints the ratio it measured rather than a sentence about it:\n2744|\n2745|```text\n2746|section coverage: bindings=56 full=1 partial=3 sliver=1 unevidenced=48 unmeasured=3 unowned=12 clauses_discharged=17/463\n2747|```\n2748|\n2749|Fifty-six section bindings discharge 17 of the 463 normative clauses their\n2750|sections carry. One binding is `full` (Section 6.2, whose single clause is the\n2751|native-Windows `conpty` requirement, discharged by the positive\n2752|`TestEveryPinnedReaderHasPositiveNativeWindowsAndWSL2Lanes` lanes together\n2753|with the negative `TestDecodeRefusesNonConptyBackendOnNativeWindows` legacy\n2754|refusal arm), three are\n2755|`partial` (Section 14.2 at 8/9, bound to\n2756|[`internal/cliresult`](internal/cliresult), whose undischarged clause `14.2#6`\n2757|is the process exit status this repository has no binary to produce; and\n2758|Section 15.1 at 5/7 and Section 15.3 at 2/3, both bound to\n2759|[`internal/axerror`](internal/axerror); the three undischarged clauses there are\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
