{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d993","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae2b-f4bb-7310-a5c5-e45123d43dca"},"sequence":2852,"recorded_at":1780531400005699,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"f3ccc2af-522d-4b28-99ba-3a506c9bdcb3","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"f3ccc2af-522d-4b28-99ba-3a506c9bdcb3","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"f3ccc2af-522d-4b28-99ba-3a506c9bdcb3"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ae4b-19f4-7490-81b4-63255b0ab445"},"task_id":"01a0ae4b-19f4-7490-81b4-63255b0ab445","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0ae4b-19f4-7490-81b4-63255b0ab445","chunk":"Read text file `README.md`.\n(2740 line(s) above)\n2741|### Measured coverage of this repository\n2742|\n2743|`tracecheck` prints the ratio it measured rather than a sentence about it:\n2744|\n2745|```text\n2746|section coverage: bindings=56 full=1 partial=3 sliver=1 unevidenced=48 unmeasured=3 unowned=12 clauses_discharged=17/463\n2747|```\n2748|\n2749|Fifty-six section bindings discharge 17 of the 463 normative clauses their\n2750|sections carry. One binding is `full` (Section 6.2, whose single clause is the\n2751|native-Windows `conpty` requirement, discharged by the positive\n2752|`TestEveryPinnedReaderHasPositiveNativeWindowsAndWSL2Lanes` lanes together\n2753|with the negative `TestDecodeRefusesNonConptyBackendOnNativeWindows` legacy\n2754|refusal arm), three are\n2755|`partial` (Section 14.2 at 8/9, bound to\n2756|[`internal/cliresult`](internal/cliresult), whose undischarged clause `14.2#6`\n2757|is the process exit status this repository has no binary to produce; and\n2758|Section 15.1 at 5/7 and Section 15.3 at 2/3, both bound to\n2759|[`internal/axerror`](internal/axerror); the three undischarged clauses there are\n2760|the RPC hello obligation `15.1#5`, the bootstrap-row sentence `15.1#6` that\n2761|binds the provider plugin rather than the host, and the hello-key and\n2762|TerminalBackend-capability prohibition `15.3#3` - this repository builds no RPC\n2763|hello frame and no provider plugin, and advertises no Structured Error as a\n2764|TerminalBackend capability. The closed 16-capability admission registry in\n2765|[`internal/terminalbackend`](internal/terminalbackend) gates which operations\n2766|an admitted probe may confer; it is never advertised on an RPC hello path and\n2767|carries no Structured Error code, so the prohibition holds vacuously and the\n2768|clause stays undischarged. The same package carries the Section 4 lifecycle,\n2769|attach, entrypoint, replication, and historical-translation conformance\n2770|harness (`conformance.go`, exercised by `conformance_test.go`) and an\n2771|AST-derived refusal-arm inventory (`refusal_arm_inventory_test.go`) that\n2772|requires every production refusal arm to be declared with a resolving named\n2773|asserting test in both directions; behavioral proof stays with each row's\n2774|named test, which the inventory resolves textually),\n2775|one is\n2776|`sliver` (Section 10.3, whose chunk offset invariant is\n2777|enforced by `validateBlobDescriptor` while its two receiver clauses have no\n2778|implementation), three are `unmeasured` (Sections 7.3, 13.14.5 and 15.2, each of\n2779|which carries a gap saying why the scanner measures zero and what is missing),\n2780|and forty-eight are `unevidenced`. Twelve sections are recorded unowned.\n2781|All 13 sections added by v0.6.0 name pending task owners in the reviewed\n2782|registry gaps; these assignments grant no runtime admission. The\n2783|[adoption ownership map](internal/traceability/adoption-v0.6.0.md) separates\n2784|shared runtime APIs, their callers, product conformance and upstream source\n2785|publication validators, and preserves historical acceptance obligations.\n2786|Assigned-scope admission therefore succeeds today for `-section 6.2` and\n2787|nothing else; every other assignment is refused with its ratio and its gap.\n2788|A `partial` binding is refused by assigned-scope admission exactly like an\n2789|`unevidenced` one: admission requires `full`.\n2790|\n2791|One admitted binding out of fifty-six covers a single clause, and it is\n2792|disclosed here rather than hidden: without Section 6.2 the admit path would only\n2793|ever be exercised synthetically. Its discharge is no longer positive-only: the\n2794|native-Windows lanes carry the positive arm and\n2795|`TestDecodeRefusesNonConptyBackendOnNativeWindows` the legacy refusal arm,\n2796|both registered against the `config-versioned-readers` acceptance case.\n2797|\n2798|That is a disclosure of the shipped state, not a target that was met.\n2799|`TestRunRefusesEveryAssignedSectionThatOnlySlivers` and\n2800|`TestVerifyAssignedSectionsRefusesEveryBindingThatOnlySlivers` pin every failing\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
